\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar on track for steep weekly losses\b0\par\par\uc2 642 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2016\par 04:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Rapid drop vs yen leads to speculation of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 * 1-Month Dollar/yen volatility soars to highest since June 2013\par \par \uc2 By Lisa Twaronite\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 12 (Reuters) - The dollar nursed losses on Friday that have put it on course for steep weekly drops against major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with many investors favouring the perceived safe-haven appeal of the yen amid sinking global markets.\par \par \uc2 Japanese markets were closed for a public holiday on Thursday, when the dollar fell as low as 110.985 yen, its lowest level since October 2014.\par \par \uc2 It last stood at 112.32 yen, above a session low of 111.88 but still down 0.1 percent and on track to shed nearly 4 percent for the week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar's overnight jump back above the 112-yen level led to speculation that Japanese authorities were checking \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, a step that often precedes \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A government official declined to comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday.\par \par \uc2 "Recent exchange-rate moves have been rough. We're closely watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market moves with a sense of urgency," the official said, on the condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso adopted stronger rhetoric, saying Japan would take appropriate actions as needed, and said he hopes the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  finance leaders gathering in Shanghai later this month will consider a global policy response in the wake of the recent market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 With the G20 looming, Japanese authorities might think twice before taking steps to stem their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strength\par \par \uc2 "I think 110 sounds terrible, for the Japanese economy," said Masashi Murata, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for \uc2 Brown Brothers Harriman\uc2  in Tokyo. "But it's a tough job for them, to keep levels in dollar/yen."\par \par \uc2 The yen's recent rapid ascent followed the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's move to adopt negative interest rates on Jan. 29, under which banks have to pay interest on certain deposits held at the BOJ. The dollar hit a high of 121.70 yen, before risk aversion, slowing Chinese growth and falling crude oil prices sent investors into perceived safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "It now appears that 110 is the line in the sand for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and while that rate seemed far away a few days ago, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair came very close to testing that level last night," Kathy Lien, managing director of BK Asset Management in New York, said in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 "Even though we are trading above that rate now, the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is significant," she said.\par \par \uc2 One-month dollar/yen implied volatility - an indicator of how much \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movement is expected in the weeks ahead - surged to 15.9 percent on Friday, its highest since June 2013 and nearly twice as high as 8.27 percent recorded earlier this month. It was last at 15.465 percent.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  did little to help the greenback in her second day of testimony before U.S. lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 While she said she still expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to gradually hike interest rates this year as the labour market and economy continue to improve, she reiterated that policymakers were not on a "pre-set" path to return policy to "normal" given a worsening meltdown in global stock markets.\par \par \uc2 The euro edged down 0.1 percent to $1.1308 but was not far from its overnight high of $1.1377, its loftiest peak since October 2015. It was on track for a weekly gain of 1.3 percent.\par \par \uc2 The dollar index, which gauges the U.S. unit against a basket of six major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , inched about 0.1 percent higher to 95.666, poised for a 1.4 percent weekly loss, after skidding to a low of 95.236 overnight, its lowest since October. (Editing by Simon Cameron-Moore) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-12T04:50:35.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160212ec2c004v4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
