\par\par \b \uc2 IFR Markets ForexWatch Asia Regional Daily Briefing\b0\par\par\uc2 1,444 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Februar 2016\par 00:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SYDNEY, Feb 12 (IFR) - Derisking persists despite JPY's NY hiccup\par     \par Market Briefs  \par     * US Jobless Claims fell 16K To 269K in February 6 Week, vs 281k Rtrs f/c\par     * Fed's Yellen: USD strength signal of US econ strength, econ creating jobs\par despite drag from strong USD\par     * Fed's Yellen: Weak oil mostly negative on US econ growth so far, on\par balance good for econ\par     * Fed's Yellen: Still evaluating negative rates, not automatic would be\par workable in US\par     * UAE energy ministers ready to cooperate on production cuts (WSJ) oil\par rallies off lows\par     * Yen surges 2 percent vs dollar as global worries deepen, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par worries mount\par     * USD/JPY rallies to flash high above 113.00 from 111.00 low, BOJ has no\par comment on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields plunge, fed fund futures price out any move by Fed in\par 2016\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 : High-yield turmoil of 2015 to carry on as market volatility\par persists\par     * Bank and resources slump sees European shares slide to 2-1/2 year low\par     * USD/MXN rises to high 19.4480 despite 2 rounds of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , reverses\par after UAE production cut story\par     * Reuters Poll: Even chance of more ECB QE in March; deposit rate cut to\par minus 0.40 pct \par \par Macro Themes in Play\par Bank stocks drag markets lower, markets discovering unintended consequences of\par NIRP (a tax on banks) and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  'policy divergence' (too strong USD)\par Yellen fails to admit Fed misread global impact of USD strength, sticks to\par script in repeat of yesterday's testimony, gives equity/commodity markets\par nothing useful; in rebuke STIR market begins pricing rate cuts\par Oil crushed to new contract lows, \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  production cut rumors go nowhere; gold\par flies on safety bid\par USDJPY down hard but finishes off lows on chatter (unconfirmed) of BOJ buying;\par EUR closes above Oct 2015 \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  meet levels; Cable sideways but cross up to 1 year\par highs\par CAD, AUD down with commodities but hold in relatively well; MXN melts down\par despite \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  buying\par     \par Looking Ahead - Economic Data (GMT)\par     * 23:50  JP Foreign Bond Investment        w/e   -85.4b-prev\par     * 23:50  JP Foreign Invest JP Stock        w/e   -364.1b-prev\par     * 00:30  AU Housing Finance*               Dec  f/c 3%, 1.80%-prev\par     * 00:30  AU Invest Housing Finance*        Dec  0.70%-prev\par     * 02:00  JP TR IPSOS PCSI                  Feb  42-prev\par     * 02:00  AU TR IPSOS PCSI                  Feb  51.2-prev\par \par  \par Looking Ahead - Events, Other Releases (GMT)\par     * 22:30  AU  RBA Governor Stevens appears before the House of\par Representatives' Standing Committee on Economics in his twice yearly\par parliamentary testimony\par \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Summaries\par  \par EUR/USD \par     * Sharp lift off 1.1280 area in Europe's morning as USD/JPY & risk dive\par     * 1.1360 neared before pullback toward 1.1305/10 into NY, goes bid in early\par NY\par     * EUR/JPY spike up helps pair near 1.1370, back down on risk bounce\par     * Stocks lift & USD gains help pair back to 1.1305/10 but buyers lurk\par     * 1.1380 neared as equity mkts give up bounce & set new session lows\par     * Pair near 1.1360 late in the day as risk remained soured\par \par  \par USD/JPY\par     * USD/JPY's o/n low at 110.99 was followed by an early NY spike to 113.04\par     * Rumors of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it was not confirmed & looks unlikely\par     * Relatively tighter range above 111.66 after that spike vs the 113.60 O/N\par high\par     * Ltd breach of 111 likely got some shorts looking to book profits\par     * L-T H&S top is the main pattern w prior key props at 113.31 now rsst\par     * 61.8% of the 110.76-125.86 rise at 110.35 is the next tech support\par     * The H&S measured objective is at 107.26\par     * GBP/JPY broke its 200-WMA at 162.60 intraday; 156.33-75 M-T targets\par     * EUR/JPY took out this & last yrs' lows w a 125.80 low; well above on close\par     * US Retail Sales the top data event Fri. Japan returns from holiday.\par \par  \par GBP/USD\par     * GBP/USD ends Noram at 1.4462 -0.4% as oil weakens into NorAm close\par     * Cable slid to low at 1.4383 in early NY after US claims data missed f/c\par     * Pair helped lower in Europe by weak USD/JPY & GBP/JPY flows, later\par reversed\par     * EUR/GBP reversed early NorAm high at 0.7898, as EUR rallied after JPY yaw\par     * Relative interest rates remain in focus, UK rate futures push out BOE\par hikes \par     * UK rates above zero favors stronger GBP despite ongoing Brexit fears\par  \par \par  \par USD/CHF\par     * USD racks up near 6% decline vs the CHF since Jan 29\par     * 4-mth low of 0.9661 as safe haven flows bolster CHF: Mkt on SNB alert\par     * Clearer drop below 0.9725 200-DMA, but close below awaited \par     * EUR/CHF's tumble fm Feb 4 1.12 peak & 76.4% of Jan '15 range\par     * Cross bounced on SNB Jordan's comments & touted bid\par     * SNB's Jordan told Bilanz doesn't rule out further steps on negative rates \par     * CHF overvalued, no EUR/CHF target (or floor)\par     * Said tying CHF to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  basket doesn't make sense\par     * Swiss Jan CPI steady at -1.3% y/y as expected\par \par  \par USD/CAD  \par     * O/N range 1.3884/4013, Noram range 1.3909/4018, Cl 1.3934, NY -46 pips\par     * Brent crude -0.15%, WTI -1.7%, Alum, +0.34%, copper -0.9%, gold +3.95%\par     * AUD/CAD +0.1%, 0.9888, CAD/JPY -1.09%, 80.51, EUR/CAD +0.52%, 1.55807\par     * DXY -0.37% (-0.07% in NY) US stocks -1.8/-0.5% (S&P -0.4% in NY trade)\par     * UST/CA 2yr -6.6 bp (+28.0) USD fell- WSJ report UAE says \f28 \uc2 \f2 OPEC\f28 \uc2 \f2  agree cut\par     * Cda new HPI +0.1%, US wkly claims -16k Fri- US retail sls, U-Mich\par [page:2417]\par \par  \par AUD/USD  \par     * Pair trades at the mercy of JPY moves in Europe & NY sessions\par     * Sharp drop in Europe's morning to 0.6984 as AUD/JPY dives near 77.60\par     * Slight JPY weakness sees lift, pair opens NY near 0.7040, AUD/JPY near\par 78.40\par     * Bout of JPY weakness spikes AUD/JPY toward 80.00, AUD/USD lifts above\par 200-HMA\par     * 0.7110 neared but lift runs out of gas as JPY firms again, pair near\par 0.7080 late\par     * RBA's Stevens speaks to House of Reps Standing Cmmty of Econ. a risk in\par Asia\par     * Impact may be limited as general risk theme dominates\par \par  \par NZD/USD  \par JPY activity drives the pair in Europe & NY, sharp drop in Europe's morning\par NZD/JPY dive from 75.25 takes NZD/USD from 0.6680 to 0.6586\par JPY strength abates, bounces sees NY open near 0.6650, JPY sharply weakens\par NZD/JPY spikes above 75.30, NZD/USD follows & lifts near 0.6700\par Pair manages to hold most NY gains & sits near 0.6685 late\par NZ Jan food price index due but general risk theme to drive pair in Asia\par  \par LATAM\par     * USD/MXN tripped stops above 19.00 w/weak oil, Ends NY well bid by high\par 19.38\par     * \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  sells USD 400 mio in 2 \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  barely a speed bump\par     * Light gamma above remains may push USD higher, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Banxico\f28 \uc2 \f2  risks losing\par control\par     * USD/BRL off 2%, ends NorAm 4.10, Bovespa down 3.5%, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  flows lwr vs prev\par     * Corruption lingers, Brazil police arrest ex-pres of construction company\par  \par     * USD/CLP flat ahead of exp'd BCCh rate hold, despite copper off 1%\par \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 : who wants to come and play?\par The sharp decline on USD/JPY over the last few days has fed nervousness over\par possible BoJ/\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . This sparked a sharp USD/JPY rally today of\par over two big figures, with explanations ranging from BoJ rate checking to\par illiquidity. We see one probable and two unlikely scenarios on USD/JPY. First,\par the G7 is unlikely to extend co-ordinated support to Japan to help deal with a\par stronger JPY (still historically weak). Neither the US nor G7 has an interest\par right now. Second, the BoJ/MoF can conduct unilateral \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but history\par is littered with failed attempts even when monetary policy is aligned with any\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  objective. A third and a more likely option is that the BoJ will be keen to\par highlight an effective implementation of negative rates from next week. If there\par is any \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , it is likely to be via agent names rather than the BoJ\par unless USD/JPY moves in a disorderly manner below 105. Related\par \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-14T23:28:38.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160211ec2b00y9d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
