\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Hits 3.5-month Low Vs. Euro As Investors Lose Faith In Central Banks\b0\par\par\uc2 711 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2016\par 22:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 By Joseph Adinolfi, \uc2 MarketWatch\par \par \uc2 Euro rises to highest level against the buck since October\par \par \uc2 The dollar weakened against the euro and yen Thursday as investors lost faith in the ability of central bankers to spur growth and stabilize markets.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a 15-month low vs. the yen, and a three-and-a-half month low vs. the euro early in the session but trimmed its declines as the day wore on.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 ICE\uc2  U.S. dollar index , a measure of the buck's strength against a basket of six rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was down 0.4% at 95.4830.\par \par \uc2 In the years since the Great Financial Crisis, investors expected too much from central bankers by believing loose monetary policy could ignite a sustainable pick-up in growth,said Kit Juckes, global FIC strategist at \uc2 Societe Generale\uc2 , in a note to clients.\par \par \uc2 Now investors are paying the price.\par \par \uc2 "Keeping policy too easy, for too long and boosting asset markets in the vain hope that this would deliver a sustainable pick-up in demand has meant that even a timid attempt at normalizing Fed policy has caused two months of mayhem," Juckes said.\par \par \uc2 Investors found little comfort in Federal Reserve Chairwoman \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's two days of testimony before Congress this week. Instead, investors are worried about the possibility the Fed might introduce negative interest rates to the U.S., said Neil Mellor, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNY Mellon.\par \par \uc2 "The fear is that [adopting negative rates] would be the Fed saying we failed to normalize policy," Mellor said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Some investors believe that the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have weakened its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling a large chunk of yen in the market Thursday.\par \par \uc2 After weakening to a low of Yen111 early in the session, the dollar abruptly surged to Yen112.23, where it remained in recent trade.\par \par \uc2 Read: Chart shows exact moment the BOJ drove the yen lower ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/chart-shows-exact-moment-the-boj-drove-the-yen-lower-2016-02-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/chart-shows-exact-moment-the-boj-drove-the-yen-lower-2016-02-11}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 The move followed comments from Masatsugu Asakawa, a top Japanese finance official, that the Japanese government would monitor the markets to see if speculative interest was behind the recent run-up in the yen.\par \par \uc2 Read: The yen has crossed a critical 'line in the sand' ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-yen-has-crossed-a-critical-line-in-the-sand-2016-02-09"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-yen-has-crossed-a-critical-line-in-the-sand-2016-02-09}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Read:Worried about stocks? Keep an eye on the yen ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/worried-about-stocks-keep-an-eye-on-the-yen-2016-02-10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/worried-about-stocks-keep-an-eye-on-the-yen-2016-02-10}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the euro traded at $1.1323 late Thursday in New York after briefly touching its highest level in more than three months earlier in the session. The shared \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at $1.1282 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    The pound   traded at $1.4473 late Thursday, compared with $1.4541 Wednesday. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Follow the day's market action through the \f28 \uc2 \f2 MarketWatch\f28 \uc2 \f2  live blog (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.marketwatch.com/thetell/2016/02/11/stock-market-live-blog-global-equity-rout-intensifies-yields-plunge-yen-soars/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.marketwatch.com/thetell/2016/02/11/stock-market-live-blog-global-equity-rout-intensifies-yields-plunge-yen-soars/}}}\uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  cuts rates\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swedish Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut its repo rate to negative 0.5% (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/sweden-cuts-main-interest-rate-further-below-zero-2016-02-11-54851335"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/sweden-cuts-main-interest-rate-further-below-zero-2016-02-11-54851335}}}\uc2 \f2 ) from negative 0.35% as low inflation persisted. The Swedish krona tumbled against the dollar on the news, with one dollar buying 8.4346 krona.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 In other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  news, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Thomas Jordan\f28 \uc2 \f2 , chairman of the Swiss National Bank, said policy makers there haven't ruled out taking rates deeper into negative territory amid fears renewed economic turmoil in the eurozone could strengthen demand for the Swiss's franc. His remarks, which will be published in the Swiss business magazine Bilanz (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/snb-chairman-not-ruling-out-further-rate-cuts-2016-02-11"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/snb-chairman-not-ruling-out-further-rate-cuts-2016-02-11}}}\uc2 \f2 ) on Friday, drove the franc lower against the euro and the dollar.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Read:The gold market just lost its best measure of Chinese demand (\f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-gold-market-just-lost-its-best-measure-of-chinese-demand-2016-01-28"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/the-gold-market-just-lost-its-best-measure-of-chinese-demand-2016-01-28}}}\uc2 \f2 )\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 11, 2016 16:01 ET (21:01 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160211ec2b003uz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
