\par\par \b \uc2 CHRONOLOGY-History of Japanese  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2016\par 16:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Feb 11 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were jarred on Thursday by concerns \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly to cap this month's 9 percent surge in the yen - its strongest gain since the 2008 banking crisis.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last round of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , conducted in the months after a massive earthquake and nuclear disaster in 2011 drew no major objections internationally, despite running against a G7 consensus that major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should float freely.\par \par \uc2 The following is a chronology of moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the 1980s:\par \par \uc2 Oct 31, 2011 - The last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the BOJ embarked on a massive monetary expansion under new chief Haruhiko Kuroda. The yen fell from a record high of 75.30 per dollar.\par \par \uc2 Aug. 4, 2011 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb gains that officials fear threaten to derail recovery from an economic slump triggered by March's earthquake. The yen falls from 76.98 to 80.25 yen.\par \par \uc2 March 18, 2011 - G7 nations jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen strength when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spikes against the dollar after a massive earthquake.\par \par \uc2 Sept. 15, 2010 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years after the U.S. dollar hits a 15-year-low of 82.87 yen.\par \par \uc2 October 2008 - As the global financial crisis hits home, the yen hits a 13-year high of 90.87 vs the dollar, prompting the G7 to issue a statement singling out the yen in warning on market volatility. No \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  follows.\par \par \uc2 March 2004 - The end of a 15-month campaign to curb the yen's rise in which Japan spend a total of 35 trillion yen, or more than $300 billion, on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 May-June, 2002 - \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen, often supported by the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  and \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The yen continues to gain against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Sept 2001 - BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen after the September 11 attacks on U.S. \uc2 The ECB\uc2  and New York Federal Reserve both operate on behalf of BOJ.\par \par \uc2 January 1999 to April 2000 - \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BOJ) sells yen at least 18 times, including once via the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and once via \uc2 the ECB\uc2 , due to worries strong yen will choke off an economic recovery. Yen continues to strengthen.\par \par \uc2 April-June 1998 - With yen weakening, BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , eventually backed by U.S. authorities.\par \par \uc2 April 1994 - August 1995 - United States \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly, often in concert with Japanese and individual European central banks, to prop up dollar. The last coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with European banks in this period takes place on August 15, 1995.\par \par \uc2 February 1987 - Louvre Accord to strengthen the dollar.\par \par \uc2 September 1985 - Plaza Accord to weaken the dollar. (Reporting by Anirban Nag and Patrick Graham) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-2-11T16:39:20.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160211ec2b00lgr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
