\par\par \b \uc2 Thailand's SET Falls on Oil-Related Losses -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,548 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2016\par 11:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 1010 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Oil-linked stocks and telcos lead declines in Thailand, Thursday, driving the benchmark SET Index down 1.8% to a close of 1280.74. \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) and Thai Oil (TOP.TH) are among the weaker performers, ending down 6.5% and 4.7%, respectively, while telcos \uc2 Total Access Communications\uc2  (DTAC.TH) and \uc2 True Corp\uc2 . (TRUE.TH) decline 6% and 6.3%, respectively. There are a smattering of earnings announcements. Thaicom (THCOM.TH) gains 8.8% after its report, while \uc2 Big C Supercenter\uc2  (BIGC.TH) and Thailand Iron Works (TIW.TH ) fall 1.2% and 2.2%, respectively, after reporting quarterly results. (jake.watts@wsj.com; @jmwatts_) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 1008 GMT Erste Bank lowers its 2016 inflation forecast for Hungary in light of lower-than-expected data for January. Mostly due to lower oil prices, Erste now sees this year's headline inflation at 0.7% versus its 1.3% previous forecast, says economist Gergely Urmossy. He expects the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to also revise lower its 2016 inflation forecast of 1.7% in March, at the publication of its next Inflation Report, and adopt additional measures to loosen monetary conditions further via unconventional measures. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1002 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2 's key trade for the current conditions in the eurozone is going long core, short-end periphery, prefering Spain to Italy at the five-year maturity, strategist Chris Attfield says. "This gives a small yield pick-up, and we think financial sector concerns and equity weakness both play worse in Italy," he says. As for Portugal, Portuguese government bonds have been so aggressively sold that "we prefer not to get involved at these levels," Mr. Attfield says. To the backdrop of poor Italian stock performance and concerns over the financial sector, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  recommends selling 30-year BTPs versus Germany. That all said, \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  keeps its long 10-year Ireland position. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0959 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The Japanese yen continues to strengthen late Thursday in Asia, reaching as strong as 110.98 yen to one U.S. dollar. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , last at 111.32 yen to one greenback, has gained almost 5% since the end of last week and has been trading at its strongest levels in more than one year, as investors snap up safe-haven assets amid another bout of selling in equities. The yen gained 1.8% against the dollar on Thursday alone. "This move in the yen may now be going dangerously quickly," Kit Juckes, strategist at \f28 \uc2 \f2 Societe Generale\f28 \uc2 \f2 , writes in a note. "When momentum slows, it will be time to take profits on yen longs, at least temporarily." Japan's stock market was closed for national holiday on Thursday but has lost 7.6% in the past two days alone as the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strengthens. A stronger local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  hurts the competitiveness of Japan's exporters and poses challenges for the Japanese government, which has been attempting to revive the sluggish domestic economy through a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (chao.deng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0949 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's largest bank, \f28 \uc2 \f2 State Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500112.BY), is down 3.3% to 153.70 rupees after it set aside more money for bad loans than expected, data that came out in its third-quarter earnings reported Thursday. Asset quality deteriorated during the quarter as the bank partially accounted for the impact of a stressed account review conducted by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Reserve Bank of India\f28 \uc2 \f2 , said Mumbai broker Reliance Securities. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  conducted a centralized review of stressed loans at Indian banks recently. If a borrower delayed a certain number of repayments or defaulted on loans at a particular bank, it would affect his or her standing in other banks' books, according to the system. This took away the leeway banks had to manage data on bad borrowers, something the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had been warning about. (kenan.machado@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0949 GMT A resilient business model and "comfortable" solvency prompts \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kepler Cheuvreux\f28 \uc2 \f2  to raise its recommendation on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Groupe BPCE\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds to buy from hold. The brokerage likes the rise in core equity tier 1 ratio, as well as the expected increase in the overall solvency ratio that should reach 18% in 2019 to abide by TLAC requirements. The group is looking to raise EUR13-17 billion via mid/long-term senior debt, as well as EUR1-3 billion through Tier 2 issues in 2016. Covered bonds should total EUR6-8 billion. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0945 GMT USD/JPY slides further, dropping around 2% on the day to hit a fresh 15-month low around Y111.01. Analysts say this will raise serious concerns that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  could be set to take action to stem yen strength. "Policy action may be imminent in Japan, given where markets are trading," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts say. Earlier this week, analysts at \f28 \uc2 \f2 HSBC\f28 \uc2 \f2  said direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market was a "major threat" with USD/JPY below 115. "The growing event risk is that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  directly in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market," they said. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0940 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Experiments that \f28 \uc2 \f2 China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are making to wean itself from the current benchmark interest-rate system, including an interest-rate corridor, could encourage more international market discipline, bolster monetary policy transparency and help improve China's credit-pricing mechanism, said BNP Paribas Investment Partners economist Chi Lo. "However, achieving market-driven interest rates could be a tall order in the short-term," he said in a report. "Despite an ostensible completion of interest rate liberalization, there are still hidden interest-rate controls, with the benchmark interest rates and administrative directives still dominating capital allocation." (mark.magnier@wsj.com; Twitter: @MarkMagnier) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0932 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP slipped Thursday, closing lower following the dovish tone struck by Fed chairwoman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2  at her appearance before the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The weakness of other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in late trade moderated the USD/PHP slide, helping it rebound from an intraday low 47.35. "We'd likely see a dollar rebound tomorrow [Friday] as other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  surrender recent gains," a local bank trader says. USD/PHP closed at 47.45 Thursday after settling at 47.47 on Wednesday. Volume is light. Traders expect the USD/PHP to move within the 47.20-47.60 range in the near-term. (cris.larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0931 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 PostNord\f28 \uc2 \f2  may have to deal with dropping mail volumes and pressure on the logistics business, but its Swedish-krona denominated bonds look well-positioned, says Swedbank. The postal company's krona issues are priced at fair levels relative to its peer group, which includes Nordic government-related entities. Swedbank keeps its marketweight recommendation on \f28 \uc2 \f2 PostNord\f28 \uc2 \f2  bonds. However, the company's credit metrics could potentially deteriorate as the postal market remains challenging. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0925 GMT Today's decision by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 , to cut its repo rate to -0.5% from -0.35%, shows it is prepared to set aside worries over a housing market bubble and strong domestic demand in order to respond to very low inflation and policy easing by other central banks, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "We think that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is still likely to need to take further action," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Capital Economics\f28 \uc2 \f2  adds, noting inflation is unlikely to pick up any time soon and other central banks are likely to loosen monetary policy further in the coming months, so recent falls in the krona are unlikely to be sustained. "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a lot more work to do before it can rest easy." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0920 GMT The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's decision to cut the repo rate by 15 bps to -0.50% might not be the last move lower, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is currently investigating 'whether it is possible within the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operational\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  monetary policy framework to implement other measures to underpin repo rate cuts.' These technicalities may, in our view, open up for further repo rate cuts down the road," says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  now sees the interest rate bottoming out at -0.53% in 3Q 2016 and staying there until 2Q 2017 when the first rate hike is forecast. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  again cut its inflation forecast, but \f28 \uc2 \f2 Nordea\f28 \uc2 \f2  notes that with persistent low global inflation and difficulties bringing up domestic inflation, "there's a risk that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Riksbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  yet again is too optimistic on the inflation outlook longer out." (dominic.chopping@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 11, 2016 05:10 ET (10:10 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160211ec2b0015w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
