\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Buys ETFs for Sixth Straight Session as Stocks Plunge -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 2,974 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2016\par 10:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0919 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  says it has bought exchange-traded equity funds for a fifth-straight session Tuesday, although it stopped short of increasing the purchase amount from the recent daily average of Y33 billion ($283 million). But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's persistent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the share market doesn't seem to be having much effect amid global market turbulence, with the Nikkei Stock Average index ending the day down 5.4%, the biggest percentage drop in two-and-a-half years. The BOJ has stepped into the exchange traded fund markets for 14 days so far this year, which brings the total number of days of purchases to 228 since April 2013. That was when the BOJ embarked on aggressive monetary easing to defeat deflation and generate 2% inflation. The BOJ has bought nearly Y6 trillion in ETFs since the start of the easing program in terms of book value, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's data. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Snippet corrected at 0933 GMT. Original mistakenly said the BOJ bought them for a sixth straight session.\par \par \uc2 0913 GMT \uc2 Sweden's National Debt Office\uc2  on Thursday launches a new, June 2026-dated inflation-linked bond at an auction to the tune of EUR1 billion. \uc2 Nordea\uc2  analysts calculate that the fair value on the break-even inflation curve is at 14 basis points above that of the June 2025-dated Swedish linker, which corresponds to a yield of 12 basis points above that of the 2025-dated linker. The 2025-dated linker is currently trading at a yield of around -0.73%, according to \uc2 Tradeweb\uc2 . (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0908 GMT The risks are skewed for USD/JPY to move below Y114.00 today, says ING. USD/JPY slid to a 15-month low around Y114.21 in Asian trade. It has since recovered and now trades at Y115.42. Steep yen gains have sparked talk the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may opt to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . But ING believes the bar is "now much higher for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 " and while USD/JPY remains above 110.00 verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and monetary easing measures are more likely. "Modest jawboning and a minor policy move is unlikely to be enough to stem the large JPY safe-haven flows in force," says ING. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0859 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's announcement of its ability to pay additional tier 1 bond coupons should reassure investors about the bank's credit in the near term, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Kepler Cheuvreux\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The German bank says its payment capacity will be enough to pay coupons on AT1 debt in 2016 and 2017. Lack of clarity on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2 's AT1 coupons is what consolidated market concerns over the banking sector in general, Kepler adds. The 6% contingent convertible bond from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  is covering most of its Monday losses today. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0857 GMT The sluggishness of European covered bonds over the past few months is now driving their strong outperformance over senior debt in February, says ING. Covered bonds have even lost traction versus seniors in some jurisdictions since the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's purchase program began, it adds. The iBoxx EUR Banks Senior index is widening 12 bps this month, while the iBoxx EUR Covered index is up by a single basis point. These adjustments should normalize senior and covered bonds' relative performance, unless covereds see more primary market action, ING adds. Covered bonds are typically viewed as a safer asset than senior unsecured issues. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0843 GMT By the beginning of the week, the Turkish lira lost ground and depreciated to the 2.94 region as the global-sell off intensified, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Garanti Securities\f28 \uc2 \f2 . On the domestic macro front, the industrial production figures for December were released as 4.4%, slightly above the market expectations. "However, the data had no impact on the course of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," says Garanti. "On Tuesday, there is no significant event scheduled at home and we think that the USD/TRY pair is likely to swing with the global concerns," says Garanti. USD/TRY last trades up 0.14% at 2.9514. (Yeliz.candemir@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0828 GMT Concerns about the state of the European banking system are limiting euro gains, RBC analysts say. The yen and the euro have gained most in recent periods of risk aversion, but the euro's gains have lagged those of the yen. "The state of the European banking system is being watched closely on the back of recent record losses being announced," RBC say. "So far there are no signs of it spilling over into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but it may explain why the rise in EUR is contained, even as JPY rallies hard." EUR/USD is down 0.1% at $1.1178, EUR/JPY falls 0.25% to Y129.04. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0825 GMT Global core bonds had another very strong run as panic in riskier markets spread rapidly but KBC analysts say it is simply confidence that is flowing away at high speed. According to the analysts, the markets reflect the feeling "that central bankers, who were also the loyal servants of markets, are out of bullets and ideas." They say the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  experiments with negative rates "as if it is doing an innocent chemical experiment somewhere in the backyard during a BBQ." (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0825 GMT Germany's industrial production data from December, showing a 1.2% fall on the month, "underlines that German manufacturing is increasingly suffering from the weakness in emerging markets," says Commerzbank economist Ralph Solveen. He notes, however, that December figures tend to be strongly influenced by how the Christmas holidays fall. "The actually rather positive orders and sales figures give reason to expect a significant recovery of production in January," Mr. Solveen says. That said, the economy probably expanded only slightly in 4Q 2015, he adds. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0813 GMT The bonds of French pharmaceutical \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanofi\f28 \uc2 \f2  may be trading at tight spread levels, but \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  keeps its marketweight recommendation given the positive outlook. The bank likes \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanofi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's diversified drug pipeline, which includes several "blockbusters," as well as the rising share of biological drugs. The group's senior bonds have been running ahead of the iBoxx EUR Healthcare index over the past 13 months. \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  expects the refinancing of a May-maturing EUR1.5 billion 4.5% issue. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sanofi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's bonds should fluctuate only moderately after its mixed 2015 results, it adds. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0804 GMT EUR/GBP hits a one-year high as sharp falls in equities and financial stocks hurt sterling, as well as ongoing concerns about the risk of the U.K. voting to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The euro also benefits from safe haven flows. EUR/GBP trades 0.3% lower at 0.7736, having risen as high as 0.7789, its strongest since January 2015. The euro pares gains, however, after data shows an unexpected drop in German industrial production in December, along with a fall in exports. U.K. trade data is due at 0930 GMT. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0758 GMT Surprisingly weak German industrial production and export data released earlier in the day are "a painful reminder that not all is hunky dory in the eurozone's largest economy," says ING economist Carsten Brzeski. While Germany's industry had been able "to stomach the cooling of the Chinese economy, the slowdown of emerging markets, the euro crisis and geopolitical risks, it now seems as if extremely low oil prices and the slowdown of the U.S. economy are simply two risks too much," he cautions. A strengthening euro exchange rate also threatens to dent exporters' performance, other economists say. Official data showed that German industrial production in December dropped 1.2% from the preceding month, in adjusted terms; exports fell 1.6% in this period. (nina.adam@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10 Feb 2016 04:29 ET \par Correction to BOJ Buys EFTs Market Talk (on Tuesday)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  bought exchange-traded equity funds for a fifth straight session Tuesday. "BOJ Buys ETFs for Sixth Straight Session as Stocks Plunge -- Market Talk," at 0919 GMT, mistakenly said the BOJ bought them for a sixth straight session.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0927 GMT Hungary's headline inflation is forecast to have accelerated on the year in January mostly due to a low reading a year earlier. This is despite a government-mandated cut in the value-added tax for pork cuts to 5% from 27% on Jan. 1 and a 5% monthly drop in oil prices, 13 analysts said in a WSJ poll. Annual inflation is seen at 1.2% and the monthly price growth at 0.1%, versus December's +0.9% and -0.3% respectively. Inflation is seen reaching the 3% target only by the end of 2017. The inflation data are due at 0800 GMT Thursday. (margit.feher@wsj.com @margitfeher) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0923 GMT U.K. industrial output data are due at 0930 GMT. Sterling is likely to be driven by broader risk sentiment, but the release could have an impact if it comes well outside of expectations. Industrial output is forecast to be down 0.2% on the month in December. RBC analysts say this is close to the estimate the U.K. statistics office used in their preliminary estimate of 4Q GDP. "A significantly different outturn" could pose "marginal risks" to that (GDP) estimate," they say. GBP/USD is up 0.1% at $1.4470, EUR/GBP is down 0.3% at 0.7781, having hit a one-year peak around 0.7852 on Tuesday. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0920 GMT Portuguese government bonds are vulnerable due to the sovereign's credit rating, say \f28 \uc2 \f2 RBS\f28 \uc2 \f2  analysts. "This means it has fewer natural buyers since many investors cannot buy non-investment grade debt and it [Portugal] is not included in a number of bond indexes," they say. They add that the domestic investor base of Portuguese government bonds is far less deep than that of Italy or Spain. Portugal is rated junk by S&P, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Fitch Ratings\f28 \uc2 \f2  and \f28 \uc2 \f2 Moody's\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and only DBRS rates it investment grade. A downgrade by DBRS would strip Portugal of its last investment grade, potentially affecting bond purchases by the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Several bond indexes include only countries with at least two investment grade ratings. Portugal's 10-year bond is trading at 3.33%, compared with 2.84% at end-January and 2.53% at end-2015, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tradeweb\f28 \uc2 \f2  data. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0906 GMT Real estate companies are drawing the spotlight in the primary euro corporate bond market this week as supply has fizzled amid dampened sentiment. There was no corporate bond supply in Europe on Tuesday--the first time this has happened since January 4, says Raiffeisen. However, Germany's Alstria Office could place a senior bond this week, the bank adds. Meanwhile, Austria's \f28 \uc2 \f2 CA Immo\f28 \uc2 \f2  is launching a seven-year retail bond Wednesday, targeting mostly domestic investors. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0902 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP ended weaker Wednesday, tracking the greenback's slide ahead of Fed Chairwoman Yellen's testimony before the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Congress\f28 \uc2 \f2 . "Everyone is expecting to hear a dovish tone from Yellen tonight," said a local bank trade, "if she's extremely dovish, then we'll say hello to 46." The USD/PHP is at 47.47 after settling Tuesday at 47.65 in moderately heavy volume. Traders expect the USD/PHP to move within the 47.20-47.60 range in the near-term. (cris.larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0857 GMT Recent sharp losses posted on Germany's DAX stock market index don't hint at a severe growth slowdown of Germany's economy, says Martin Wansleben, managing director of German Chambers of Commerce, or DIHK. Germany's benchmark index fell sharply over recent days along with other key indexes. Investors were worried about the health of the global economy and the plight of energy companies as oil prices move lower. Uncertainty also remains over the pace of U.S. interest-rate tightening. (andrea.thomas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0856 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's industrial output likely contracted for the second-successive month in December, after floods in the southern Indian city of Chennai--an auto-manufacturing hub--hit production and overseas demand was weak. Production likely fell 0.1% from a year earlier, according to the median estimate in a poll of 13 economists by The Wall Street Journal. Output had contracted 3.2% in November. "We estimate India's industrial production growth to stay in negative zone in December, as suggested by sluggish growth in infrastructure industrial output," \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rupa Rege Nitsure\f28 \uc2 \f2 , group chief economist at L&T Finance Holdings, says in a research note. The data is due Friday. (anant.kala@wsj.com; @anantvkala) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0841 GMT The USD index hit a 3.5 month low on Tuesday and "looks vulnerable" before testimony by Federal Reserve Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 , say ING analysts. "Markets will be sensitive to remarks concerning financial conditions having tightened." ING think the USD index can fall to 95. It trades down 0.1% at 95.98. EUR/USD "can creep a little higher" but $1.13/$1.15 "should prove medium term sell," the ING analysts say. EUR/USD trades 0.3% lower at $1.1266. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0839 GMT Italian utility \f28 \uc2 \f2 Enel\f28 \uc2 \f2  hits a relative value wall, as its bonds are now looking too expensive versus better-rated peers, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The bank downgrades its recommendation to marketweight from overweight. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Enel\f28 \uc2 \f2 's senior bonds are trading flat to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Electricite de France\f28 \uc2 \f2  and German EnBW, which \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  sees as unjustified. It favors RWE's 1.875% March 2020 bond, which offers a 40 bps z-spread pick-up over \f28 \uc2 \f2 Enel\f28 \uc2 \f2 's 4.875% March 2020 issue. However, not everything looks bleak for the Italian group's bonds as its 2015 results were better than expected, it remains supported by \f28 \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  buying and its hybrids could benefit from a potential S&P upgrade to BBB+. (tasos.vossos@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0835 GMT Germany's economy is stable but growth will slow somewhat in 2016, the managing director of German Chambers of Commerce, or DIHK, says. The lobby group forecasts 1.3% economic growth for this year, unchanged from its forecast given in autumn and despite a pick-up in companies sentiments. The forecast is more pessimistic than the government's expectations of 1.7% growth for 2016. Germany's economy grew 1.7% in 2015. "This is a solid performance, although not quite as dynamic as the 1.7% in the year before," says Martin Wansleben, DIHK managing director. "The multiple international and national risks stand in the way of stronger growth. We can also not expect that oil prices and the euro will fall as much as in the past year." (andrea.thomas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0828 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The steady decline in the consumer price index and faltering economic growth may see Singapore's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ease its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy again in April, \f28 \uc2 \f2 BMI Research\f28 \uc2 \f2  says. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore\f28 \uc2 \f2  eased its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  policy in October by allowing the local unit to appreciate at a slower pace against a basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . BMI says that in April, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may "re-center" the Singapore dollar's nominal effective exchange rate band lower, which would mean a one-off devaluation of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . If the MAS eases, it will be the third such move in 15 months. "The recent leg down in oil prices, the potential for consumer prices to remain in deflation for a second straight year" will be the factors the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will consider, it says. The house expects the USD/SGD to average S$1.4600 in 2016. The pair is currently at S$1.3930. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 February 10, 2016 04:29 ET (09:29 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160210ec290011e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
