\par\par \b \uc2 Thailand's SET Slides Slightly Despite TMB Recovery -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,478 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juli 2015\par 12:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2015, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1019 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] It's another quiet day for market-moving corporate news in Thailand, where the SET index ends 0.1% lower at 1486.74. TMB Bank (TMB.TH) recovers by 4.4% from recent losses that put its stock price not far from its lowest since May 2014. Telco Total Access Communications (DTAC.TH) also rebounds, ending up 2.8%, following local news reports about possible changes to its mobile concession conditions. Among losers is Central Pattana (CPN.TH), down 2.6%, and \uc2 Airports of Thailand\uc2  (AOT.TH), down 2.3%. (jake.watts@wsj.com; @jmwatts_) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: DWT \f28 \par \par \uc2 1018 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--Commenting on Chinese GDP data, Trevor Greetham, head of multi asset at investment firm Royal London, says "from a global stock market point of view China's slowdown is good news just as Japan's weakness was good news in the 1990s." He says that "a steady drop in Chinese demand will see commodity prices drop, keeping inflation low and monetary policy loose elsewhere in the world." (josie.cox@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1014 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Vietnam's trade deficit in June narrowed from the previous month as exports rose while imports declined. The country incurred a trade deficit of $140 million in June, lower than a government deficit forecast of $700 million and narrowing from a deficit of $1.24 billion in May, Vietnam Customs Department said. Exports in June rose 4.6% on month to $14.325 billion, while imports fell 3.2% to $14.465 billion, the department said. For the first half of this year, exports rose 9.3% on year to $77.77 billion, while imports were up 16.7% to $80.84 billion. (trong-khanh.vu@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @TrongKhanhVu) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1013 GMT The latest data on jobs and earnings from the U.K. indicate the economy is nearing full employment, says Brewin Dolphin Group head of research \f28 \uc2 \f2 Guy Foster\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Unemployment ticked up by 7,000 in the three months to May and wage growth accelerated, according to official statistics. Mr. Foster says the U.K. is enjoying a "Goldilocks scenario" of subdued inflation and robust growth. He adds that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials may be tempted to start tentatively raising interest rates later this year, perhaps in November. (Jason.Douglas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1012 GMT The latest U.K. jobs market data suggest productivity is poised to pick up, says Capital Economics. Chief U.K. economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Vicky Redwood\f28 \uc2 \f2  says the mix of a small rise in unemployment in the three months to May and a sharp pickup in wage growth suggests firms are focusing on getting more out of their workforce rather than hiring extra hands. That should spur productivity growth, she says. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials have been waiting anxiously for a revival in productivity growth to keep a lid on inflation as the economy nears full employment, so today's data may reassure officials that such a recovery is in train. Investors expect a rate rise in mid-2016. (Jason.Douglas@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0959 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] China's aggressive attempts to stem falling stock prices have drawn fire from free-market believers, but Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda seems to think it is unfair to label China as an unusually radical \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventionist\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . "I don't think it is appropriate to say China is the only country doing something quite unique," Kuroda says at a press conference. Kuroda is right. The BOJ is now the biggest single investor in Tokyo share markets, thanks to aggressive equity funds purchases launched in 2013 by Kuroda himself. Also in the 1990s, Japan deployed various tools to lift a sliding share market, such as having postal savings buy more stocks, urging firms to increase dividends and pressuring traders not to sell shares. Indeed, China's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has sparked a flood of tweets and commentaries in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  calling it the equivalent of Tokyo's past "price-keeping \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operations\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ." (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0955 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Commercial real-estate lending in the U.K. is fast losing its attractiveness, according to CBRE. The broker estimates the average risk-adjusted returns for senior commercial real-estate lending made in the second quarter will be 3.7% per year. Says this is 1% lower than six months ago. "For banks, returns on risk-weighted assets are approaching the level of around 2% where they may not meet cost of capital hurdles; for other lenders, the relative value play that enticed them into the sector has narrowed noticeably. We may therefore be approaching a point in the market when lenders' resolve is tested," says Dominic Smith, head of real estate debt analytics at CBRE. "Lenders may want to resist further downward pressure on margins to stabilise returns, or the requirement to place capital may force them to accept lower margins and higher risk as the price of winning business." (art.patnaude@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0942 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields are off the lows seen in the wake of Tuesday's disappointing retail sales data and are steady in Europe ahead of Fed Chair \f28 \uc2 \f2 Janet Yellen\f28 \uc2 \f2 's first semi-annual monetary policy statement before Congress Wednesday. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commerzbank\f28 \uc2 \f2  says she is likely to use the opportunity to further prepare the market for the fact that a first rate hike before the end of the year is quite possible, albeit still data dependent. The 10-year \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Treasury\f28 \uc2 \f2  yields 2.41%, compared with 2.399% late Tuesday. (gary.stride@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0932 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The USD/PHP is higher Wednesday, tracking the greenback's advance around the region. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  pair is at 45.215 after settling at 41.195 Tuesday. Volume is moderately heavy. "The greenback remains strong against our regional counterparts and the recent focus back on the U.S. as market players await what Yellen has to say," said Jonathan Ravelas, market strategist at BDO Unibank. Traders expect the USD/PHP to stay within the 45.00-45.40 trading range in the near-term. (Cris.Larano@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0919 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bluebay Asset Management\f28 \uc2 \f2  has begun to close out some of the hedges against Greece it put in place in futures and swaps markets earlier this year, given that the risk of a near-term Greek exit has diminished, according to \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Riley\f28 \uc2 \f2 , the firm's head of credit strategy. "We've started to add back some risk and close out some of the hedges, but not completely," he says. Commenting on the recent deal with Greece, "At first blush, this looks like a worse proposal than could have been secured by the Greek government before the referendum. So it's not an obvious sell and time is tight," he adds. Bluebay significantly reduced bets on so-called peripheral government bonds in May, mainly due to fears over Greece. (christopher.whittall@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0917 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Greece's parliament is broadly expected to approve measures to unlock a fresh international bailout Wednesday, but strategists and investors remain cautious, saying that the crisis is far from over. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Rabobank\f28 \uc2 \f2  rates strategists write in a note that "implementation risks and austerity fatigue leading to missed targets and reform delays remain a clear likelihood." They add "the longer term sustainability of Greece's debt burden and the ambitious nature of the bailout proposals are likely to remain causes for concern." (josie.cox@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0906 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Bangkok-based Krungsri Securities expects Thailand's policy rate to remain flat in the second half of 2015 despite weeks of market turmoil over Greece and China. Krungsri notes that the slower economic growth reflects a decline in Thailand's exports, a slowdown in government spending, and high household debt. After cutting policy rates twice in quick succession to 1.5% earlier this year, \f28 \uc2 \f2 the Bank of Thailand\f28 \uc2 \f2  has already taken action to address the bleak picture. However, Krungsri notes, "the economic situation is worse than that caused by the 2011 flood crisis and 2014 coup." It predicts that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could opt to cut rates again if the economy worsens. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: ELM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 July 15, 2015 06:20 ET (10:20 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020150715eb7f0014d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
