\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW-Ex-IMF Shinohara: Weak yen won't cause " \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  war" with U.S.\b0\par\par\uc2 507 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2015\par 14:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 * Shinohara says weaker yen good for Japan economy\par \par \uc2 * Yen fall due to divergent US, Japanese monetary policies\par \par \uc2 * BOJ needn't ease further or fret (Adds comments on Fed, BOJ)\par \par \uc2 By Tetsushi Kajimoto and Yuko Yoshikawa\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 18 (Reuters) - The yen's fall against the dollar will not cause a "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war" between Japan and the United States, as it stems from the two nations' diverging monetary policies, a former top official of the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  and \uc2 Japan's Finance Ministry\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Naoyuki Shinohara, an IMF deputy chief until last month and Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat before that, said on Wednesday he had not heard much concern from the U.S. administration over the yen's decline, even as the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hovers near eight-year lows to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose last week above 122 yen, the highest since mid-2007, on expectations for the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  to raise U.S. interest rates as soon as June, while speculation continues that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will expand its massive monetary stimulus.\par \par \uc2 The weaker yen "won't be a big problem as it stems from different positions on monetary policy," Shinohara, vice finance minister for international affairs from 2007 to 2009, told Reuters. "It would be a different story if (\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) were to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to target \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 He added, "It won't lead to the kind of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war that was seen in the past," referring to friction between the two countries decades ago, when critics accused \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  of huge yen-selling market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and benefit exporters.\par \par \uc2 The yen's fall has delivered hefty profits to Japanese exporters by making their products more competitive, but it has also boosted the cost of imports.\par \par \uc2 Japanese officials, who initially welcomed the yen's fall after Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  took office in December 2012 and adopted loose monetary and fiscal policies, have recently been noting the problems as well.\par \par \uc2 Shinohara said a weaker yen was positive for the overall economy, but policymakers needed to watch effects on individual industries.\par \par \uc2 He predicted the Fed would not raise rates until the autumn or later, and that further dollar gains would stir more concerns about volatile emerging markets rather than yen impact.\par \par \uc2 Japan may not see inflation reach the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of 2 percent until after 2017, but there is no need for it to expand monetary stimulus now, he said.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ should not stick to its two-year timeframe for achieving 2 percent inflation but treat it as a medium-term target, Shinohara said.\par \par \uc2 "Markets won't be convinced just by setting 2 percent inflation as a sacrosanct goal and pledging to do whatever it takes," he added. "To make markets believe what you say, you have to set a goal that looks feasible from the markets' perspective." (Additional reporting by Leika Kihara; Editing by William Mallard and Clarence Fernandez)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-3-21T13:05:11.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150318eb3i00h1y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
