\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-U.S. official:  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's QE is not the same as  \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 292 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Februar 2015\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2015 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details, comment from official)\par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL, Feb 10 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's use of aggressive monetary stimulus to kick-start its economy is different from a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at driving down its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a senior \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  official said on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 The official, who was speaking to reporters on the sidelines of the G20 meeting of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors and finance ministers in Istanbul, also said there appears to have been progress in recent days on a package for Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The issue of 'competitive devaluation' has been a divisive one in recent weeks, reflecting concern that Japan and Europe's use of quantitative easing (QE), or aggressive stimulus, was aimed at making exports cheaper.\par \par \uc2 While the United States has already called on members of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  leading economies to stick to commitments on exchange rate policy, the official said Japan was not attempting to manipulate the yen \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "There's a difference between a country like Japan putting QE kinds of policies in place than if they were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in building up reserves to drive down the value of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the official said, speaking on condition of anonymity.\par \par \uc2 "They are not the same policies."\par \par \uc2 Tokyo has embarked on rounds of massive stimulus to revive an economy hamstrung by years of deflation. However, the U.S. official also said that Japan should not be too reliant on such measures, and should also focus on structural reform.\par \par \uc2 There appears to have been some recent progress on an international package to support Ukraine, the official said, without giving further details.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by David Dolan; Editing by Nick Tattersall) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2015-2-10T14:56:47.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020150210eb2a00i7n\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
