\par\par \b \uc2 Lots of Action but Taiwan Dollar Ends Little Changed -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,625 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2014\par 09:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0844 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/TWD is little changed, as exporter sales offset foreign investor buying, say two local traders. The pair closes at 31.290--its highest onshore closing level in over 50 months, versus 31.285 late Monday; they say the local \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is believed to have bought the U.S. dollar around 31.210 (versus 31.200 Monday) to keep the pair in its target band. The USD/TWD stayed below 31.200 in the early morning due to a weaker USD/JPY, but sharp gains in the USD/CNY then triggered buying from importers and foreign investors and lifted the USD/TWD. "With Chinese yuan deviating from the rising Korean won and Japanese yen, it was hard to find a clear direction for the Taiwan dollar," a trader says. Taiwan shares end 0.6% lower Tuesday; foreign investors have been net sellers of local stocks for three straight sessions. (fanny.liu@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0841 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] India's widening current account deficit in the last quarter is not alarming as the country's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are comfortable, says Finance Minister Arun Jaitley. "Since the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves in the country [are] comfortable and the balance of payment is also broadly under control, I don't think there is any reason to take the kind of steps which we had to take in 2013," says Jaitley tells upper house of parliament. India's current account deficit in the three months ended September 30 nearly doubled to $10.1 billion from $5.2 billion a year earlier as gold demand rose after authorities lifted restrictions on its imports. The government would consider putting curbs on non-essential imports such as gold if the deficit rises beyond comfort level, he adds. (prasanta.sahu@wsj.com; \uc2 Twitter\uc2 : @pksahu9) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0837 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Czech inflation in November slowed a touch on-year from the month before, and prices contracted on a monthly basis, creating a risk that the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may delay an exit from ultra-loose monetary policy, says Raiffeisenbank economist Michal Brozka. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  aims to keep interest rates at near-zero levels and the koruna weak vs the euro until at least early 2016. But Mr. Brozka says in light of falling oil prices and a surplus of foodstuffs in Europe that weighs on food prices, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may keep the policy unchanged into the second half of 2016. (sean.carney@wsj.com, @SeanCarneyWSJ) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0833 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] State-run power generator \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Thermal Power Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2  (NTPC) (532555.BY) Tuesday said it has signed two loan agreements totaling 30 billion rupees to part fund its investment programs. The New Delhi-headquartered company signed a 15-year loan of 20 billion rupees with \f28 \uc2 \f2 HDFC Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (500180.BY) and 10 billion rupee loan with the Syndicate Bank (532276.BY). NTPC has a total electricity generation capacity of 43.12 gigawatts and is building power projects with a generation capacity of over 23 gigawatts. It plans to have a generation capacity of 128 gigawatts by 2032. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0827 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's government will likely cut spending by about $12 billion this fiscal year to ensure there isn't a slippage in achieving its fiscal deficit target, senior officials say. Most of the cuts would take place in areas such as the construction of roads, railways and power projects. The officials say execution of these projects has been slow because of a late federal budget as the country went to polls this year. However, spending on welfare programs such as guaranteeing rural employment or providing food subsidies would not be lowered, they add. The spending cuts are essential to narrow a budget deficit to 4.1% of gross domestic product in the year through March 2015 from 4.5% last year. India cut spending in the previous two years also to contain the deficit. (prasanta.sahu@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @pksahu9) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0822 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] India's oil ministry says the price of its imported crude oil basket fell to $65.60 a barrel by the end of Monday's trade from $66.98 on Friday, reflecting volatility in global crude prices. Crude-oil futures sank in Asian trade Tuesday, extending their losses to levels not seen in more than five years with market participants showing little confidence that the market will find a bottom soon. Oil prices have slumped since the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries decided to leave its oil output unchanged. A fall in crude-oil prices is good for India as the country imports three-quarters of its energy needs. (saurabh.chaturvedi@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @journosaurabh) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0819 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Austria completes its government bond issuance for this year Tuesday, offering EUR880 million of the 1.65% October 2024 bond at an auction later in the day. The small volume of the auction is likely to support demand, and so will possibly German bond redemptions this week totaling EUR14 billon, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2 's fixed income strategist Chiara Cremonesi. She adds that \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  likes the 10-year area of the Austrian yield curve versus the shorter maturities, in particular versus the five-year segment, but it doesn't like this maturity versus the extra-long end of the year. Ms. Cremonesi also says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2  considers the 10-year Austrian bond as expensive versus other core countries. Auction results are due at 1000 GMT. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0807 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may step into the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to buy the yen if the USD/JPY pair goes above 125, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  chief Tokyo \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist Taisuke Tanaka. "The dollar has risen 20% in just four months against the yen. If the dollar goes above 125 yen in the near term and brings negative effects on the domestic market, it is very possible that the authorities would take some countermeasures," he says, adding that verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the MOF would start when the USD/JPY hits around 125. In the past, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has done dollar-selling, yen-buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  when the pair was above 125 in 1991, 1992, 1997 and 1998, he says. The pair is at 119.60. (takashi.mochizuki@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @mochi_wsj) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0800 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--A long, long time ago in a galaxy far, far away, there were no reliable Spanish house price indexes. That changed with the 2008 start of the ongoing property bust, and now there are too many: INE said Tuesday 3Q house prices rose 0.3% Y/Y, which is a tad contradictory with the -2.5% Y/Y reading provided for the same period by the Public Works ministry, late last month. There is no clear explanation for the diverging views, especially since the ministry data is believed to be a better reflection of real-time price movements. How to break the tie? Fotocasa's prestigious own index has a 6.5% Y/Y drop for the 3Q; as of Nov, Fotocasa estimates that the average used home in Spain is EUR105,000 cheaper compared with the 2007 peak. (david.roman@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0757 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--\f28 \uc2 \f2 Sweden's National Debt Office\f28 \uc2 \f2  publishes its third and final forecast for this year, and monthly data suggest that the debt office is likely to lower its forecast for central government borrowing for this and next year, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 Citigroup\f28 \uc2 \f2  economist Tina Mortensen. Up until November, government borrowing has been around SEK13 billion lower than forecast, with tax revenues being SEK15 billion higher than expected, she says. The release is due at 0830 GMT. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0735 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ]--Despite headwinds from faltering European demand, unexpectedly strong September manufacturing numbers, and a November manufacturing PMI which came in at a 4-month high, point to ongoing recovery in the manufacturing sector. The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2  survey forecast for October industrial production is +0.2% on the month and +1.8% on the year, against +0.6% and +1.5% respectively, while manufacturing output is seen +0.2% m-m and 3.2% y-y vs +0.4% and +2.9%. Data released 0930 GMT. GBP/USD trades at 1.5664. gary.stride@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0728 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The average spot price of liquefied natural gas Japan imported in November was $14.4 per million British thermal units, slightly lower from October's $15.3/mmBtu, data from the Ministry of Economy, Trade and Industry (METI) show. Spot LNG prices in Asia have been falling mirroring this year's broad decline in energy markets, and due to abundant supply as several new producers coming to market including the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Exxon Mobil\f28 \uc2 \f2  (XOM) led PNG LNG. Since METI started announcing the monthly data in spring, the price has fallen 21% from $18.3/mmBtu in March, according to the data. Prices are unlikely to rally unless this winter turns out to be very cold. (mari.iwata@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 December 09, 2014 03:44 ET (08:44 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020141209eac9000tv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
