\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar Stronger Against Yen After \uc2 OPEC\uc2  Decision\b0\par\par\uc2 By Hiroyuki Kachi   \par \uc2 735 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 November 2014\par 07:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Korean (English)\par \uc2 RTNWK\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar strengthened against the yen in Asian trade Friday, with lower oil prices among the factors accelerating the selling of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 As of 0450 GMT, the dollar was at Y118.29 from Y117.74 late Thursday in New York, amid thin trading due to the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday.\par \par \uc2 Following a decision by the \uc2 Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries\uc2  to keep intact its established production targets despite the recent sharp falls in crude prices, Nymex West Texas Intermediate crude tumbled below $70 a barrel for the first time in four years.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 OPEC\uc2  decision gave an upward bias to the greenback that spread to trading in Asia.\par \par \uc2 "Oil price weakness is a direct boon to the U.S. economy," said Shinji Kureda, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading group at \uc2 Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The resulting improved sentiment about the U.S. recovery was reflected in Tokyo share prices, which gained traction from the opening bell. The Nikkei Stock Average was up 1.2% midway through the afternoon session.\par \par \uc2 Traders also cited buying by Japanese importers related to commercial transaction settlements ahead of the regular book closing at the end of the month.\par \par \uc2 "There are investors who have no choice but to buy (the dollar), even though they don't really want to," at this level, said Yuzo Sakai, manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  business promotion at Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  & Ueda Harlow.\par \par \uc2 Some traders and analysts also noted the latest fall in Japan's inflation rate.\par \par \uc2 Japan's annual rate of inflation moved further away from the 2% level targeted by Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  in October. Growth in the core consumer price index fell last month to 0.9%, providing more bad news for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The inflation figure strips out volatile fresh food prices and is adjusted for a sales tax increase in April.\par \par \uc2 "That maintains expectations for additional monetary easing by the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , though nothing immediate is expected," said Yuji Saito, executive director of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  department of \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 A fall in Japan's two-year government bond yield into negative territory for the first time ever, provided another catalyst for the dollar's strength against the yen. Expectations for a widening gap between U.S. and Japanese interest rates has been one of the drivers of the yen's decline against the greenback.\par \par \uc2 "I think the negative yield on the two-year note can be cited as one reason behind the yen weakness," said Akito Fukunaga director of bond research at \uc2 Barclays\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 With the dollar gaining momentum again, verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities is likely if the greenback comes closer to the Y120 threshold, said \uc2 Credit Agricole\uc2 's Mr. Saito, who expects the dollar will likely move in a Y117.00-Y119.50 range during next week.\par \par \uc2 In other \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading, the euro was at $1.2447 from $1.2466, while the euro was at Y147.26 from Y146.74.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index, a measure of the dollar against a basket of major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was up 0.29% at 80.72.\par \par \uc2 Interbank \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rates At 00:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                             Latest         Previous   %Chg   Daily     Daily   %Chg \par                                            2150 GMT           High     Low    12/31 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    USD/JPY Japan           118.29-30      117.69-75  +0.49   118.33   117.72 +12.33 \par    EUR/USD Euro            1.2447-50      1.2465-69  -0.15   1.2467   1.2446  -9.43 \par    GBP/USD U.K.            1.5707-10      1.5733-41  -0.18   1.5740   1.5706  -5.13 \par    USD/CHF Switzerland     0.9654-58      0.9638-44  +0.15   0.9658   0.9642  +8.13 \par    USD/CAD Canada          1.1348-54      1.1329-38  +0.15   1.1353   1.1330  +6.86 \par    AUD/USD Australia       0.8492-94      0.8543-47  -0.61   0.8547   0.8490  -4.73 \par    NZD/USD New Zealand     0.7830-32      0.7864-69  -0.45   0.7874   0.7828  -4.75 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Euro Rate \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    EUR/JPY Japan           147.24-26      146.72-81  +0.33   147.31   146.76  +1.74 \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Source: \f28 \uc2 \f2 ICAP PLC\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Hiroyuki Kachi at Hiroyuki.Kachi@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 28, 2014 00:57 ET (05:57 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 28-11-14 0656GMT\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNWK00020141128eabs0000k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
