\par\par \b \uc2 Yamasaki named as Japan's top financial diplomat\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juli 2014\par 04:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2014 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 4 (Reuters) - A Japanese official who's long worked on global financial issues will become the country's vice finance minister for international affairs, the government said on Friday.               \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Tatsuo Yamasaki, 56, will take over from \uc2 Mitsuhiro Furusawa\uc2 , who will retire, on Friday as part of a routine personnel reshuffle, indicating no change in policy.               \par \par \uc2 Like many of his predecessors as Japan's top financial diplomat, Yamasaki has been director-general of the MOF's International Bureau.               \par \par \uc2 Yamasaki joined the ministry in 1980 and has spent most of his career at the international bureau, supervising areas such as development policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. He served as director of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  division in 2002-2004, during which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  spent about 35 trillion yen ($344 billion) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's strength.               \par \par \uc2 The new vice finance minister is expected to pursue the line of the \uc2 G7\uc2  and G20 to adhere to market-set exchange rates and a policy that is not targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He will take charge of issues ranging from \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to policy coordination with other countries including the G20.               \par \par \uc2 Masatsugu Asakawa, deputy vice minister for policy planning and co-ordination at the MOF, who has liaised with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , will take over from Yamasaki as international bureau chief.               \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in November 2011 to prevent a strong yen from derailing an export-led recovery. The yen weakened by about 20 percent versus the dollar last year due to Japan's reflationary policies.               \par \par \uc2 Released: 2014-7-4T03:43:48.000Z   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020140704ea740010p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
