\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 486 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 15:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par POLITICAL DEAL ON EU BANKING UNION COMPLETED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  struck a deal on the final leg of its banking union after all-night talks, closing the chapter on a key project that it is hoped will prevent eurozone banking crises from bankrupting entire countries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CREDIT AGRICOLE PLEDGES STRONG PROFIT RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  pledged to increase its net profit heavily over the next two years, as it seeks to draw a line under a prolonged period of restructuring in the aftermath of Europe's sovereign debt crisis. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S MARUBENI PLEADS GUILTY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese trading company Marubeni agreed to pay an $88 million fine and pleaded guilty to foreign-bribery charges in the company's second foreign-bribery payout in three years, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Justice Department\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNB MAINTAINS MINIMUM EXCHANGE RATE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  repeated its pledge to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to prevent the Swiss franc from strengthening beyond 1.20 per euro, saying the floor is still the "right tool" to curb upward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ KURODA SAYS WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF RISKS EMERGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Kuroda reiterated that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't hesitate to adjust to its monetary policy if risks emerge that make it difficult for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to achieve its 2.0% inflation target. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUNICH RE\f28 \uc2 \f2  WARNS OF LOWER 2014 PROFIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Munich Re\f28 \uc2 \f2  forecast consolidated profit of \u8364\'20\'AC3 billion for this year, below the \u8364\'20\'AC3.3 billion reached last year, citing a higher tax burden, lower investment returns, average claims costs and moderately lower rates it can demand from its customers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CFTC SEEKS COMMENT ON IMPROVING SWAPS DATA STREAM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seeking advice on ways to resolve a series of data problems that have hobbled efforts to see more clearly into the multitrillion-dollar swaps market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIGHTSQUARED COMMITTEE MEMBER SAYS PLAN TREATS ERGEN FAIRLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A member of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 LightSquared\f28 \uc2 \f2  committee overseeing the company's restructuring options said that the wireless venture's reorganization plan treats Dish Network Chairman Charlie Ergen fairly. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MORGAN STANLEY\f28 \uc2 \f2  BROKER, LAW CLERK CHARGED WITH INSIDER TRADING \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A Wall Street stockbroker and a managing clerk at a law firm face federal charges the two engaged in an insider-trading scheme that netted $5.6 million in illegal profits. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FRENCH COURT UPHOLDS SENTENCE FOR ROGUE TRADER \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 France's highest appeals court said that former \f28 \uc2 \f2 Soci\u233\'00\'E9t\u233\'00\'E9 G\u233\'00\'E9n\u233\'00\'E9rale\f28 \uc2 \f2  trader J\u233\'00\'E9r\u244\'00\'F4me Kerviel must serve the three-year prison sentence handed to him for his wayward bets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par VISTA NEARS $3 BILLION FOR LATEST TECH BUYOUT FUND \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Vista Equity Partners\f28 \uc2 \f2 , a San Francisco private equity firm focused heavily on the software industry, expects to attract as much as $3 billion in initial commitments for its latest flagship fund this month, according to documents viewed by Dow Jones.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 20, 2014 10:00 ET (14:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140320ea3k00223\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
