\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Financial Services News of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2014\par 21:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par FINANCIAL SERVICES TOP STORIES \par  \par POLITICAL DEAL ON EU BANKING UNION COMPLETED \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  struck a deal on the final leg of its banking union after all-night talks, closing the chapter on a key project that it is hoped will prevent eurozone banking crises from bankrupting entire countries. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CREDIT AGRICOLE PLEDGES STRONG PROFIT RECOVERY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Credit Agricole\f28 \uc2 \f2  pledged to increase its net profit heavily over the next two years, as it seeks to draw a line under a prolonged period of restructuring in the aftermath of Europe's sovereign debt crisis. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par JAPAN'S MARUBENI PLEADS GUILTY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese trading company Marubeni agreed to pay an $88 million fine and pleaded guilty to foreign-bribery charges in the company's second foreign-bribery payout in three years, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 U.S. Justice Department\f28 \uc2 \f2  said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par INDIAN GOVERNMENT TO SELL PART OF \f28 \uc2 \f2 AXIS BANK\f28 \uc2 \f2  STAKE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Indian government\f28 \uc2 \f2  is trying to sell a stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Axis Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  that could be valued at as much as $937 million, two people familiar with its plans said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par GREECE'S NBG SWINGS TO 4Q PROFIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 National Bank of Greece\f28 \uc2 \f2 , Greece's largest lender, swung to a robust 4Q profit of more than half a billion euros thanks to a series of tax benefits carried over from earlier years that helped offset continuing large provisions for bad loans. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par SNB MAINTAINS MINIMUM EXCHANGE RATE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Swiss National Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  repeated its pledge to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to prevent the Swiss franc from strengthening beyond 1.20 per euro, saying the floor is still the "right tool" to curb upward pressure on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ KURODA SAYS WILL \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IF RISKS EMERGE \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Kuroda reiterated that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  won't hesitate to adjust to its monetary policy if risks emerge that make it difficult for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to achieve its 2.0% inflation target. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 MUNICH RE\f28 \uc2 \f2  WARNS OF LOWER 2014 PROFIT \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Munich Re\f28 \uc2 \f2  forecast consolidated profit of \u8364\'20\'AC3 billion for this year, below the \u8364\'20\'AC3.3 billion reached last year, citing a higher tax burden, lower investment returns, average claims costs and moderately lower rates it can demand from its customers. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par CFTC SEEKS COMMENT ON IMPROVING SWAPS DATA STREAM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Commodity Futures Trading Commission\f28 \uc2 \f2  is seeking advice on ways to resolve a series of data problems that have hobbled efforts to see more clearly into the multitrillion-dollar swaps market. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LIGHTSQUARED COMMITTEE MEMBER SAYS PLAN TREATS ERGEN FAIRLY \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A member of a \f28 \uc2 \f2 LightSquared\f28 \uc2 \f2  committee overseeing the company's restructuring options said that the wireless venture's reorganization plan treats Dish Network Chairman Charlie Ergen fairly.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 March 20, 2014 16:00 ET (20:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020140320ea3k0035v\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
