\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  -Yen skids to 6-month low vs dollar, 4-year low vs euro\b0\par\par\uc2 662 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2013\par 01:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Net short positions in yen climb to 6-year high in latest data\par \par \uc2 * AUD also under pressure, still pressured by RBA \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk\par \par \uc2 * Asian markets monitor China/\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions, Iran developments\par \par \uc2 By Lisa Twaronite and Ian Chua\par \par \uc2 TOKYO/SYDNEY, Nov 25 (Reuters) - The dollar rose to a six-month high and the euro pushed to a new four-year peak against the yen in Asian trading on Monday, as investors positioned for yen weakness after speculators had bet on further yen declines.\par \par \uc2 Positioning data last week showed \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculators increased net short positions in the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the most in six years, reflecting a belief the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will stay the most aggressive in maintaining its massive stimulus program among major central banks.\par \par \uc2 "Stops were triggered in dollar/yen, which triggered stops in euro/yen," said Bart Wakabayashi, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 State Street Global Markets\uc2  in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "It does seem a bit overdone," he said, with no specific macroeconomic move to which the jump can be attributed.\par \par \uc2 Market participants cited the reluctance of some investors to be short dollars ahead of this week's U.S. Thanksgiving holiday on Thursday. Demand was also seen from Japanese importers, as Monday was a "gotobi" date, or a multiple of five on which books are traditionally settled throughout a month.\par \par \uc2 The euro rose as far as 137.93 yen, its highest since October 2009, and was last up 0.5 percent at 137.89 yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was up 0.7 percent to 101.87 yen after climbing as high as 101.895 yen on the EBS trading platform, barrelling through the July 8 peak of 101.54 yen to its highest level since May 29.\par \par \uc2 Against the dollar, the euro slipped 0.1 percent to $1.3540 .\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Executive board member Benoit Coeure said on Monday on a visit to Tokyo that slowing price growth, or disinflation, in Europe is likely to continue for now, but will not progress to deflation because the economy is recovering and inflation expectations remain anchored at around 2 percent.\par \par \uc2 ECB Governing Council member Christian Noyer also said on Monday said that European financial markets are stabilising and interest rates are returning to normal levels.\par \par \uc2 The euro remains above last week's lows hit after a media report suggested the ECB could lower its deposit rate to negative. The report, which had since been played down by the ECB, sent the euro spiralling to a low of $1.3399 from $1.3584.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar retraced Friday's 2-1/2 month low of $0.9139 according to Reuters data, and was last at $0.9144, down about 0.2 percent on the day and still pressured by the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Reserve Bank of Australia Governor \uc2 Glenn Stevens\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Stevens last Thursday said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "open-minded" about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , having consistently argued the Aussie dollar was overvalued compared with fundamentals.\par \par \uc2 The Aussie slid 2.1 percent last week. Immediate support is seen around $0.9097, the 76.4 percent retracement of its August to October rally.\par \par \uc2 Traders said the commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could continue to struggle particularly if tensions between China and Japan grew.\par \par \uc2 China at the weekend suddenly imposed new rules on airspace over islands at the heart of a territorial dispute with Tokyo, prompting Japan and ally the United States to warn of an escalation into the "unexpected" if Beijing enforces the rules.\par \par \uc2 However, news of a breakthrough that curbed Iran's nuclear activity could help offset any potential fallout from renewed China/Japan tension.\par \par \uc2 Iran and six world powers clinched a deal on Sunday to curb the Iranian nuclear programme in exchange for initial sanctions relief.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | AUF | ABN | D | DNP | E | RBN | J | M | NAT | ND | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | SI | U | UKI | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131124e9bo000cc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
