\par\par \b \uc2 Asian Shares Higher on Positive U.S. Lead\b0\par\par\uc2 By Daniel Inman   \par \uc2 386 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2013\par 02:19\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Japanese and Australian stocks moved higher on early Friday, as barrage of positive news from the U.S. resulted in broad strength for the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Asia received a strong lead from the U.S., where the Dow Jones Industrial Average closed above 16,000 points for the first time, after Janet Yellen moved one step closer to the top job at the Federal Reserve. The Senate Banking Committee voted to approve Ms. Yellen's nomination to become Fed chairman next year - a move considered market positive as she is expected to leave the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's easy monetary policy little changed. In addition, a strong U.S. jobs report also helped sentiment.\par \par \uc2 The overnight developments helped push the dollar higher against a number of regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The greenback added a total of 1.1% against the yen on Thursday to its highest level since early July and extended its run early Friday - last at Y101.23, compared with Y101.15 late Thursday in New York.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar stabilized at US$0.9233 on Friday after dropping lower overnight. Local factors contributed to the Aussie's decline, after Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Glenn Stevens late Thursday said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was open to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on an overly strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Nikkei gained 0.8%, helped by the yen weakening below the Y101 to the dollar mark. The market added to Thursday's gains, when the benchmark index rose 1.9%, bucking broad weakness across Asian stocks.\par \par \uc2 Australia's S&P/ASX 200 rose 0.9% and South Korea's Kospi was up less than 0.1%.\par \par \uc2 Friday's gains come at an end of a week dominated by outperformance of Chinese stocks. Last Friday, Beijing released a broad outline for structural reform of the economy, which boosted Chinese stocks on Monday. Although the initial excitement is over, stocks in Hong Kong and Shanghai remain Asia's best performers for the week.\par \par \uc2 In Hong Kong, the Hang Seng China Enterprises Index is up 5.9% week-to-date and the Shanghai Composite is up 3.3% in the mainland.\par \par \uc2 Write to Daniel Inman at daniel.inman@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 21, 2013 20:19 ET (01:19 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131122e9bm0007t\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CB Financial Services Ltd: Gold inches lower as investors weigh Fed policy\b0\par\par\uc2 924 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2013\par \uc2 News Bites - Private Companies\par \uc2 NBPRCO\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2013. News Bites Pty Ltd.   \par \par \uc2 NEWS BITES - PRIVATE COMPANIES\par \par \uc2 [Company Release]\par \par \uc2 Gold futures have declined in commodities markets today (November 18th), though losses have been limited amid speculation the Federal Reserve will maintain its quantitative easing programme into 2014.\par \par \uc2 A US manufacturing index and industrial production report came in below estimates on Friday, reinforcing the view the country"s recovery is not yet secured.\par \par \uc2 Janet Yellen, who has been formally nominated to replace Ben Bernanke as Fed chair, told the Senate Banking Committee last week that there are dangers to ending stimulus too soon and indicated she would support a prolonged accommodative monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Investors are now keenly awaiting the release of the minutes from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 "s latest policy meeting, which are due to be published on Wednesday. The country"s forthcoming retail sales and consumer price reports are also likely to impact on prices.\par \par \uc2 Gold for December delivery declined by 0.2 per cent in European morning trade on the Comex division of the \uc2 New York Mercantile Exchange\uc2 , having closed 0.09 per cent higher on Friday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/18/gold-inches-lower-as-investors-weigh-fed-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 COMPANY BACKGROUND\par \par \uc2 ACTIVITIES\par \par \uc2 CB Financial Services One Financial Markets is an online broker providing 24 hour trading facilities to investors in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , indices, commodities and futures.\par \par \uc2 BUSINESS NEWS ROUND UP\par \par \uc2 18 November 2013: CB Financial Services Ltd: Dollar drifts lower versus yen despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  speculation\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The dollar has inched lower against the yen today (November 18th), easing from two-month highs despite speculation the Japanese government is set to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Last week, the country"s finance minister Taro Aso said it is important to retain the ability to step in and stem the yen"s appreciation in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading markets. His comments followed the release of data showing Japan"s gross domestic product growth slowed by more than anticipated in the third quarter on an annual basis and contributed to further weakening of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/18/dollar-drifts-lower-versus-yen-despite-intervention-speculation"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 18 November 2013: CB Financial Services Ltd: Gold inches lower as investors weigh Fed policy\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Gold futures have declined in commodities markets today (November 18th), though losses have been limited amid speculation the Federal Reserve will maintain its quantitative easing programme into 2014. A US manufacturing index and industrial production report came in below estimates on Friday, reinforcing the view the country"s recovery is not yet secured. Janet Yellen, who has been formally nominated to replace Ben Bernanke as Fed chair, told the Senate Banking Committee last week that there are dangers to ending stimulus too soon and indicated she would support a prolonged accommodative monetary policy. Investors are now keenly awaiting the release of the minutes from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 "s latest policy meeting, which are due to be published on Wednesday.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/18/gold-inches-lower-as-investors-weigh-fed-policy"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 16 November 2013: CB Financial Services Ltd: Demand for yen eases amid QE expectations\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The yen continues to hold above the 100 to the dollar level today (November 15th) and is on course to record weekly declines against all of its major \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading peers. With the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  set to meet next week to discuss possible policy changes following reports showing Japanese economic growth slowed in the third quarter, sentiment towards the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been dampened. The greenback"s gains were then extended after Janet Yellen"s nomination hearing in front of the Senate Banking Committee.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/15/demand-for-yen-eases-amid-qe-expectations"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 15 November 2013: CB Financial Services Ltd: Copper pares weekly decline following Yellen comments\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] Copper has rallied for a second session in commodities trading markets today (November 15th), after Federal Reserve chair nominee Janet Yellen said there are risks to ending the bank"s quantitative easing programme too soon. Recent data emerging from the country had led to suggestions the Fed would look to scale back its asset purchases at its December policy meeting. However, current deputy chair Ms Yellen was quizzed by the Senate Banking Commission yesterday amid her nomination for the top role at the bank and stated the stimulus should be maintained until the US labour market has "improved substantially". Copper for delivery in three months added 0.6 per cent to $7,035.25 per metric tonne on the London Metal Exchange, trimming the metal"s weekly loss to 1.9 per cent. Futures for delivery in March gained 0.6 per cent to $3.1895 per pound on the Comex division of the New York Stock Exchange. Source: Company Website\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/15/copper-pares-weekly-decline-following-yellen-comments"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 14 November 2013: CB Financial Services Ltd: Dollar advances strongly against yen\par \par \uc2 [Company Release] The dollar has reached its strongest level in two months against the yen today (November 14th), advancing in \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading markets on the back of comments from Federal Reserve nominee Janet Yellen. In a statement yesterday, Ms Yellen said the US labour market and economy are "performing far short of their potential", leading to suggestions the Fed will look to maintain its stimulus into 2014. The yen began to slide after Japan"s finance minister Taro Aso said the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will retain the option to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if required to curb excess volatility. Data released today showed the country"s economy expanded by 0.5 per cent in the third quarter, above the consensus estimate for a 0.4 per cent gain.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.onefinancialmarkets.com/market-news/2013/11/14/dollar-advances-strongly-against-yen"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here for the full original announcement}}}\par \par \uc2 Dokument NBPRCO0020131119e9bj0005l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
