\par\par \b \uc2 JGB prices edge down as Nikkei rally dulls debt appeal\b0\par\par\uc2 272 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2013\par 03:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 15 (IFR) - Japanese government bond prices inched down on Friday as a slide in the yen buoyed Tokyo shares to six-month highs and somewhat dulled the appeal of fixed-income assets.\par \par \uc2 A modest rise in U.S. Treasuries overnight had limited positive impact on JGBs, but the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's offer to buy 710 billion yen ($7.1 billion) worth of JGBs in the secondary market with residual maturities of one to five years helped support the market.\par \par \uc2 The bond-buying programme is part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's effort to prop up the economy and pull the country out of persistent deflation.\par \par \uc2 The 10-year yield added 1 basis point to 0.605 percent, while the 10-year JGB futures dipped 3 ticks to 144.99.\par \par \uc2 Tokyo's Nikkei share average climbed 1.8 percent to above 15,000 for the first time in six months, as the yen tumbled to a two-month low of 100.315 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The yen slide was driven by a risk-on mode in global markets and comments by Finance Minister Taro Aso that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must retain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a policy tool.\par \par \uc2 The 20-year JGB yield was up 0.5 basis point at 1.485 percent, while the 30-year yield edged up 1 basis point to 1.635 percent.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  is to sell 1.2 trillion yen of 20-year debt next Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-JAPAN-JGB/ | ABN | D | E | RBN | J | M | NAT | ABX | BNX | FUN | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131118e9bf0003c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex