\par\par \b \uc2 Yen Falls to Two-Month Low Versus Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ira Iosebashvili and Clare Connaghan \par \uc2 430 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2013\par 19:28\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar hit its highest level against the yen in more than two months Thursday, after Japan's finance minister said that the country should fight excessive moves in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , opening the door for more \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The greenback slipped against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, after Janet Yellen, the nominee to head the Federal Reserve, said the U.S. economy still needs support from the Federal Reserve as it continues to mend.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Taro Aso told parliament that "Japan must have tools to counter speculative moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," giving investors a strong indication that a tentative strengthening of the yen would probably be met with pushback. Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe has vowed to jolt the country's lackluster economy and fight chronic deflation, which have been partially caused by years of a strong yen.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to a high of Y101.15 against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the New York session, its strongest level since Sept. 11.\par \par \uc2 The case for BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also bolstered by a government report showing growth slowing in the last quarter, after surging earlier in the year.\par \par \uc2 "Softer data out of Japan [reinforces] the notion that the BOJ and Abe government will need to maintain and potentially increase stimulus efforts," economists at TD Bank wrote in a note to investors.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the dollar gave up earlier gains against the euro and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Ms. Yellen, currently the Fed's Vice Chairwoman, told a Senate confirmation hearing that there are dangers to ending the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's $85 billion-a-month bond-buying program too soon, despite progress in the economy. The Fed's bond purchases, which are tantamount to printing money, have weighed on the greenback while buoying the economy.\par \par \uc2 The WSJ Dollar Index inched down to 73.325 during the testimony, from an earlier intraday high of 73.557.\par \par \uc2 The pound came under pressure, falling as low as $1.5990, after U.K. retail sales unexpectedly fell 0.7% in October from the previous month. The results were weaker than expected. Economists polled by The Wall Street Journal had predicted no change on the month, and a 3.1% on-year rise.\par \par \uc2 "The data serves to remind us that the U.K. economy still faces headwinds," said Jane Foley, a G-10 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Write to: ira.iosebashvili@dowjones.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 14, 2013 13:28 ET (18:28 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020131114e9be003gw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
