\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Yen slips after Yellen hearing sparks risk rally\b0\par\par\uc2 647 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2013\par 00:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Yen hits 2-mth low vs USD, 2-wk low vs EUR, 4-yr low vs GBP\par \par \uc2 * Stock rally boosts risk sentiment, hurting low-yielding yen\par \par \uc2 * Aso's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remark adds fuel to move\par \par \uc2 * Weak euro zone GDP data knocks EUR/USD lower\par \par \uc2 By Hideyuki Sano\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 15 (Reuters) - The yen dropped to a two-month low against the dollar and a four-year trough versus sterling on Friday after Federal Reserve Chair nominee \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 's dovish remarks boosted risk appetite, undermining the low-yielding Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Yellen defended the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stimulus to spur growth and called efforts to boost hiring an "imperative", reinforcing investors' expectations that U.S. monetary stimulus may be in place for an extended period.\par \par \uc2 The dollar rose as high as 100.31 yen and last stood at 100.26 yen, up 0.2 percent from late U.S levels. The British pound soared above major resistance at 160 yen and rose to 161.14 yen, its highest level since September 2009.\par \par \uc2 Even the euro, which was knocked lower against the dollar by weak euro zone data, held its ground at two-week highs versus the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The yen can only go down now. Yes, we need to be aware of the risk of the Fed's tapering but Yellen is unlikely to do anything drastic. With the world's major central banks all having a dovish bias, we are going to see a rally in risk assets," said a trader at a Japanese bank.\par \par \uc2 Rising risk tolerance could encourage risk-averse Japanese investors to buy more foreign assets, thereby hurting the yen further.\par \par \uc2 Following Yellen's remarks, U.S. stocks hit record highs while Japanese shares jumped to a six-month high, heading for their best weekly performance since December 2009.\par \par \uc2 On the other hand, the fall in U.S. bond yields following Yellen's comments was too small to discourage investors from buying U.S. debt, thus providing little reason to sell the dollar, said Koji Fukaya, chief executive officer of FPG Securities.\par \par \uc2 "The yen seems to be the weakest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  of all at the moment. When overall financial markets are risk-on while the U.S.-Japan yield gap does not shrink much, the yen tends to weaken. The yen may keep sliding for the time being," he said.\par \par \uc2 Sentiment on the yen turned so bearish that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  even reacted to comments from Finance Minister Taro Aso the previous day that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  must retain \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a policy tool, even though he was speaking in theoretical terms.\par \par \uc2 Hardly any traders expect yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this stage after the yen has dropped almost 20 percent over the past year on Japan's aggressive monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 As the dust settles after Yellen's confirmation hearing, the dollar had mixed fortunes against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The euro slipped to $1.3453, pulling back from a one-week high of $1.3499 hit on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Investors sold the euro after figures showed the euro area economy all but stagnated in the third quarter, keeping alive expectations the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should do more to stimulate growth.\par \par \uc2 The British pound fared better, despite disappointment from UK retail sales data on Thursday, as traders bet the Bank of England would have to tighten policy much earlier than it had suggested.\par \par \uc2 The cable stood at $1.6066, not far from the week's high of $1.6101.\par \par \uc2 There is no major economic data scheduled for release in Asia on Friday. In Europe, the region's finance ministers will meet in Brussels for a second day to outline plans to deal with banks still in difficulty.\par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 / (UPDATE 1) | AUF | ABN | D | DNP | E | RBN | J | M | NAT | ND | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNP | SI | U | UKI | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020131114e9be001i8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
