\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Call 0215 GMT News Briefing\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ewen Chew   \par \uc2 470 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Juni 2013\par 04:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Newswires English Content\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Snapshot:\par \par \uc2 The risk-off tone grows more evident on a global basis, with bond yields rising and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  falling in Latin America, South Africa, Turkey, as well as in Asia. Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are still under pressure despite an overnight drop in the WSJ Dollar Index, though some in Asia such as the Singapore dollar are showing a bit more resilience. Traders expect to see more \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help stall the erosion of emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Nikkei drops as much as 2.0% on renewed yen strength, dragging regional bourses lower. The euro stays elevated after Germany affirms the ECB's independence in executing its bond-buying plans.\par \par \uc2 Levels (from previous day's close) (Intraday low/high)*:\par \par \uc2 EUR/USD: 1.3310 (Down) 1.3305/1.3317\par \par \uc2 USD/JPY: 96.51 (Up) 95.91/96.58\par \par \uc2 AUD/USD: 0.9466 (Up) 0.9418/0.9496\par \par \uc2 GBP/USD: 1.5644 (Down) 1.5634/1.5652\par \par \uc2 EUR/CHF: 1.2310 (Up) 1.2301/1.2319\par \par \uc2 *Data provided by Thomson Reuters\par \par \uc2 Heads Up:\par \par \uc2 0300 S Korea May Economic Trends, including household loans, money supply index Lf\par \par \uc2 0400 Australia Jun DEEWR Monthly Leading Indicator of Employment\par \par \uc2 0500 Japan Jun \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  Monthly Report released\par \par \uc2 0530 India Apr IIP Index of Industrial Production\par \par \uc2 0530 France 1Q Job creation\par \par \uc2 0600 Germany May CPI\par \par \uc2 0645 France May CPI\par \par \uc2 N/A Singapore 2Q MAS Survey of Professional Forecasters\par \par \uc2 N/A India May CPI rural, urban and combined\par \par \uc2 Top News:\par \par \uc2 -- \uc2 Bank Indonesia\uc2  has raised the interest rate of its overnight deposit facility 25 basis points to 4.25% with immediate effect, to help ease mounting pressures on the rupiah, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 -- The \uc2 World Bank\uc2  is concerned about the economic impact that central banks around the world may have when they start to rein in their accommodative monetary policy, the organization's president said.\par \par \uc2 -- Japanese core machinery orders fell 8.8% on month in April, the government said Wednesday, after a significant rise the previous month. The fall was slightly larger than expected by economists surveyed by Dow Jones Newswires and the Nikkei, who estimated on average that core orders decreased 8.2% from the previous month.\par \par \uc2 -- Australian consumer sentiment rose in June, rebounding from two straight months of declines, an encouraging sign as the resource-rich economy struggles to cope with an anticipated slowdown in mining investment that's expected to trigger a rise in unemployment.\par \par \uc2 -- The \uc2 German government\uc2  urged the country's highest court to throw out a legal challenge to the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government bond purchase plan, telling judges Tuesday they had no jurisdiction over the independent ECB's monetary policy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Ewen Chew at ewen.chew@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 12-06-13 0247GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130612e96c00023\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
