\par\par \b \uc2 DJ News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2013\par 05:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FIN MIN ASO: WON'T \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENE\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  IN \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FOREX\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MARKET IMMEDIATELY \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday he has no intention to order direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market to tackle the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent rebound, in a rare move for a Japanese official to publicly rule out \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  after a sharp appreciation. (published 0146 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  MOF YAMASAKI: OVERNIGHT DOLLAR-YEN EXCHANGE RATE MOVE RAPID, CLOSELY MONITORING \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A senior finance ministry official expressed concerns about overnight tumbles in the dollar against the yen, while indicating the dollar staying above Y100 would pose no major problems as long as policies are carried out for domestic reasons. (published 0222 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ABE ADVISER HAMADA: MARKETS WERE "OVERCONFIDENT" IN ABENOMICS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One of Japanese Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's economic advisers said that investors had become "overconfident" in the quick impact of Abenomics, and that "probably markets are adjusting to that excessive euphoria." (published 0139 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SCHUMER URGES U.S. TO PRESS CHINA ON ACCOUNTING ISSUES \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A U.S. senator has urged the Obama administration to press China for more cooperation on accounting-fraud investigations involving Chinese companies that are traded on U.S. exchanges. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN ECON MIN AMARI: WANT TO CAP VOLATILITY IN MARKETS BY IMPLEMENTING GROWTH STRATEGY \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's economy minister said Friday that he's confident recently volatile financial markets will stabilize as the government implements its growth strategy. (published 0156 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par JAPAN MAY 1-20 TRADE DEFICIT Y1.014 TLN; UP 34.7% ON YR \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan posted a merchandise trade deficit of Y1.014 trillion in the first 20 days of May, up 34.7% from the Y752.49 billion deficit in the year-earlier period, the finance ministry said Friday. (published 0020 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par SOUTH KOREA'S REVISED 1ST-QUARTER GDP UP 0.8% ON QUARTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The South Korean economy improved in the first quarter from the prior three months, but at a slightly slower pace than previously forecast, strengthening the case for Asia's fourth-largest economy to continue maintaining an accommodative policy. (published 2300 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: ECB OFFERS NO NEW STIMULUS, DESPITE A POORER OUTLOOK \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  took no new steps to boost the euro zone's flagging economic prospects despite forecasting an even-deeper recession this year and low inflation in 2014, putting its stimulus tools "on the shelf." (published 2341 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par GREEK PARLIAMENT VOTES TO TOUGHEN CHARGES AGAINST FORMER FINANCE MINISTER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Parliament voted Thursday to toughen the charges against a former finance minister over his handling of a list of 2,000 wealthy Greeks with Swiss bank accounts, part of a high-profile investigation that has highlighted the failure of Greek authorities to tackle widespread tax evasion. (published 2208 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: BOEHNER SAYS OBAMA BEING 'RECKLESS' WITH VETO THREAT, RISKS GOVERNMENT SHUTDOWN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 House Speaker John Boehner accused President Barack Obama of being "reckless" in threatening to veto two House spending bills in the absence of a broader budget agreement. (published 2043 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par UPDATE: JUNK BOND FUNDS SEE RECORD $4.6 BILLION OF OUTFLOWS - LIPPER \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bond funds saw waves of outflows in the week ended Wednesday, with funds dedicated to low-grade, or "junk," debt seeing record withdrawals, according to fund tracker Lipper. (published 2151 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par S&P CUTS OUTLOOK ON BRAZIL DUE TO SLOW ECONOMIC GROWTH \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Standard & Poor's\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ratings Services cut its outlook on Brazil to negative from stable, citing the South American country's slow economic growth. (published 2250 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par     ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARY ======= \par  \par  \par AUSTERITY'S NOT THE ONLY BURDEN IN EUROPE \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Arguments continue in Europe over whether governments should relax budgets to encourage growth. But some analysts argue this debate is drawing attention from something more important that is generating serious headwinds for the region's economies: Europe's broken financial sector. (published 1953 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par FED WATCH: NEW SURVEY SEES WEAKER INFLATION EXPECTATIONS \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 As actual measures of inflation drift ever downward from the Federal Reserve's 2% target, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials have been pretty sanguine. (published 1923 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 