\par\par \b \uc2 Risk-on tone set to drive US investment-grade market\b0\par\par\uc2 1,297 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2013\par 13:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 By John Balassi\par \par \uc2 May 28 (IFR) - Risk-taking is on this Tuesday morning following the long holiday weekend, with global equity indexes painting an even more positive picture than the credit indices. The Nikkei managed to stabilize after a volatile Monday session and was bid up over 1% as the yen continues to weaken on rumors of a direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Market tone for issuance momentum still looks reasonable - and that means we could well see a busy shortened week in the US high-grade market. The consensus call for volume is a brisk USD15bn to USD20bn, as some market participants said that a few larger benchmark trades were left on the table during last week's surge of volatility.\par \par \uc2 Data begin on a slow note, with the Case-Shiller home price index for March out at 9am and the latest consumer confidence survey at 10am. Economic reports pick up in the US on Thursday, when first-quarter GDP revisions and jobless claims are due, followed by Friday's Chicago PMI, consumer income and spending data. - Dow Futures: +109 S&P Futures: +12.85, Nasdaq Futures: +28.50 - CDX IG20: 2.125bp tighter, CDX HY20: 0.75 point higher - 10-yr \uc2 UST\uc2  yield: 2.043%, +3.6bp; 30-yr \uc2 UST\uc2  yield: 3.203%, +3.2bp\par \par \uc2 USD HIGH-GRADE CALENDAR\par \par \uc2 Odebrecht Offshore Drilling Finance will start roadshows this week as it looks to market a USD benchmark 144A/RegS senior secured amortizer maturing in 2022. The deal is expected to receive an investment-grade rating. \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , Itau and \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  have been mandated as global coordinators, while BB Securities, \uc2 BNP Paribas\uc2  and Santander are bookrunners.\par \par \uc2 The Republic of Korea, Aa3/A+, announced it has mandated joint leads \uc2 Citigroup\uc2 , \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , \uc2 Goldman Sachs\uc2 , \uc2 HSBC\uc2 , KDB and Woori Bank to arrange investor meetings, with a possible deal to follow.\par \par \uc2 Russian Agricultural Bank\uc2 , a 100% state-owned Russian bank rated Baa1/BBB, has mandated JPM, RBS and VTB Capital to arrange a series of fixed-income investor meetings commencing today. An international bond issue may follow, subject to market conditions.\par \par \uc2 Banco Santander Chile\uc2 , Aa3/A/A+, announced it has mandated BNP, DB, GS and Sant to arrange fixed-income investor meetings in the US, LatAm and Europe. A 144A/Reg S transaction could follow early this week.\par \par \uc2 Mexican state-owned oil company \uc2 Pemex\uc2 , Baa1/BBB/BBB, started roadshows last week, meeting fixed-income investors in the US with \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 USD HIGH-YIELD CALENDAR\par \par \uc2 Syndicate officials indicate that this week will be moderately active for high-yield supply, with most underwriters polled typically lead-lefts on two or three deals. Today is expected to be quiet, with activity picking up in the days ahead.\par \par \uc2 Global power company \uc2 InterGen\uc2 , expected rating of B1/B, will begin marketing a USD800m equivalent dual-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  two-part senior secured offering on Tuesday, with the 144A/Reg S senior secured deal to be split between a dollar-denominated 10-year non-call five tranche and a sterling-denominated eight-year non-call four. \uc2 Deutsche Bank\uc2 , \uc2 Barclays\uc2 , BofA Merrill, \uc2 Credit Suisse\uc2 , MUFJ and RBC are joint bookrunners.\par \par \uc2 OVERNIGHT HEADLINES\par \par \uc2 ECB, BoJ BOOST SHARES, DOLLAR\par \par \uc2 Investors seized on clear signs of policy support from Japanese and European central banks on Tuesday, driving world shares higher and denting appetite for safe-haven German bonds. Heightened expectations that the US Federal Reserve will soon taper its stimulus programme and a rebound in Japanese stocks saw the dollar strengthen by 1.3 percent against the yen, its biggest one day gain in nearly three weeks. Equity markets around the world have traded at their highest levels in years over the past few weeks on the back of huge stimulus measures by the Fed and other central banks, despite little evidence of strong growth in the world economy.\par \par \uc2 BANKIA SHARES TUMBLE 20% AFTER ISSUE\par \par \uc2 Shares in state-owned Spanish lender Bankia tumbled on Tuesday after billions of new shares flooded the market as part of a multi-billion euro cash injection, with little hope of a quick recovery amid tough business conditions. More than 11 billion shares issued as part of a EUR15.5bn (USD20bn) recapitalisation of the bank, in what was meant to be a new beginning after a EUR24bn bailout last year that eventually triggered a European rescue of Spain's financial system.\par \par \uc2 VALEANT TO BUY BAUSCH AND LOMB FOR USD8.7bn\par \par \uc2 Valeant Pharmaceuticals International\uc2  said on Monday it agreed to buy Bausch and Lomb Holdings Inc from \uc2 Warburg Pincus LLC\uc2  for USD8.7bn, a cash deal set to vault the Canadian company into the upper ranks of the global pharmaceutical sector. The purchase strengthens Valeant's offerings in ophthalmic pharmaceuticals, contact lenses and lens care products, along with adding ophthalmic surgical devices and instruments to its portfolio. Valeant shares rose nearly 8 percent in Toronto to CAD93.71, touching an all-time high. It had gained 13 percent on Friday following reports a deal was in the works.\par \par \uc2 US REPORT SAYS WEAPONS DESIGNS ACCESSED BY CHINESE\par \par \uc2 Chinese hackers have gained access to designs of more than two dozen major US weapons systems, a report said on Monday, as Australian media said Chinese hackers had stolen the blueprints for Australia's new spy headquarters. Citing a report prepared for the Defense Department by the Defense Science Board, the Washington Post said the compromised US designs included those for combat aircraft and ships, as well as missile defenses vital for Europe, Asia and the Gulf.\par \par \uc2 GLOBAL MACRO\par \par \uc2 - Treasury Bonds down under risk on move overnight, 10s and futures lead way lower; big volume added to by calendar roll\par \par \uc2 - The tactical bias is defensive, looking to sell into the 1.97% yield support zone in 10s; look for a 2.06% to 1.99% range in 10s\par \par \uc2 - Monitoring JGB market; key to keep long and short term rates stable; will continue with flexible market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ; 2% CPI target is flexible; economic risks still to downside; must prevent JGB yields rising on debt worries; too early to design exit strategy; expected short-term rates to gradually rise - BoJ's Miyao\par \par \uc2 - China could be downgraded if GDP falls below 6% - \uc2 Moody's\par \par \uc2 - China said looking for 7% annual growth over next decade - Premier Li\par \par \uc2 - European banks have started drawing down \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, indicating renewed confidence.\par \par \uc2 - German April Import prices -3.2% y/y vs -2.3% prev, -2.3% exp\par \par \uc2 - French May consumer confidence 79 vs 84 prev, 85 exp\par \par \uc2 - European Credit Indices tighter, iTraxx S-19 XOver moves 14.8bp higher to 385.3bp, Main improves 4.3bp to 93.8bp\par \par \uc2 - Peripheral spreads tighter again after good day Monday going in opposite direction to core again. No new lows as yet for Spain and Italy under 280bp and 250b\par \par \uc2 US DATA\par \par \uc2 09:00 S&P/Case-Shiller Home Price Index (March) (mkt +10.1% y/y, prev +9.3% y/y)\par \par \uc2 10:00 Consumer Confidence (May) (mkt 69.5, prev 68.1)\par \par \uc2 10:00 Richmond Fed Manufacturing (May) (prev -6)\par \par \uc2 10:30 D