\par\par \b \uc2 REFILE-Asian Development Bank elects Japan's Nakao as president\b0\par\par\uc2 438 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 April 2013\par 07:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Corrects day in first paragraph to Friday)\par \par \uc2 MANILA, April 26 (Reuters) - The \uc2 Asian Development Bank\uc2  (ADB) said on Friday its board of governors unanimously elected \uc2 Takehiko Nakao\uc2 , Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, to head the bank, after its former president resigned to become governor of the Bank of Japan.\par \par \uc2 Nakao, 57, will be tapping into his experience as Japan's former vice finance minister for international affairs as he faces the task of helping developing Asia tackle strong capital flows coming from easier monetary policy in advanced economies that may result in disruptive asset bubbles.\par \par \uc2 "His extensive experience in international finance and development and broad and deep knowledge of the Asian region will serve ADB well in pursuing its vision of an Asia-Pacific region free of poverty," P. Chidambaram, chairman of the ADB Board of Governors and finance minister of India, said in a statement released by the Manila-based development lender.\par \par \uc2 Nakao was the only nominee for the position vacated by \uc2 Haruhiko Kuroda\uc2 , who resigned in March to become governor of Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Shortly after he assumed office, Kuroda led the radical overhaul of the BOJ's monetary policy that stunned global financial markets, focusing on expanding the monetary base to meet its inflation target in two years.\par \par \uc2 Nakao, who has held senior positions in \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a career spanning more than three decades, will serve Kuroda's unexpired term which ends on Nov. 23, 2016. He holds an economics degree from the \uc2 University of Tokyo\uc2  and a master of business administration from the University of California, Berkeley.\par \par \uc2 He has represented Japan at the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  and \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  meetings of economic powers in the last year and oversaw \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in 2011 to stem the yen's rise.\par \par \uc2 "I would like to express my sincere gratitude to all the member countries that extended support to Mr. Nakao's candidacy," Japanese Finance Minister Taro Aso said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Japan has dominated the helm of the multilateral lender since its inception in 1966, sharing the status of largest shareholder with the United States.\par \par \uc2 Several emerging economies, emboldened by their rising clout and rapid growth, have begun questioning the tradition of advanced economies taking the top posts at global financial institutions, although Americans have managed to remain in charge at the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  and Europeans at the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Rosemarie Francisco; Editing by Matt Driskill)\par \par \uc2 ADB-PRESIDENT/ (CORRECTED) | ABN | D | E | RBN | J | M | PHD | SI | RNP | DNP   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130426e94q0005r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
