\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-MOF's Furusawa appointed as Japan's new  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  diplomat\b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2013\par 00:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 (Adds details)\par \par \uc2 * New \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official does not indicate change in policy\par \par \uc2 * Furusawa's views on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  unknown, likely to follow G7\par \par \uc2 * Outgoing \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  official in frame to lead \uc2 Asian Development Bank\par \par \uc2 By Stanley White\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, March 29 (Reuters) - International financial expert \uc2 Mitsuhiro Furusawa\uc2  will become Japan's vice finance minister for international affairs, the country's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) said on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Furusawa, 57, will assume his post on Friday, taking over from Takehiko Nakao, who is set to become the head of the \uc2 Asian Development Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Furusawa has never worked at the ministry's section directly in charge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . He has not publicly spelled out his stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy but he is likely to follow the G7 stance of adhering to market determined exchange rates while standing ready to counter excessive and disorderly \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements.\par \par \uc2 Furusawa has headed the ministry's financial bureau since August last year. He has also held posts at the ministry's international bureau, dealing with development policy as well as the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  and the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (IMF).\par \par \uc2 Furusawa's predecessors in recent years served as the ministry's international bureau chief just before becoming its top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official.\par \par \uc2 Before serving as financial bureau head, Furusawa worked at the IMF as a member of its executive board for two years. He also worked in senior roles at Japanese embassies in Paris and Washington for about two years, to 1999 and 2009 respectively.\par \par \uc2 Nakao's tenure as the top financial diplomat saw \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  several times in 2011 to prevent the yen's rise from derailing an export-led recovery in the aftermath of the devastating March 2011 earthquake and tsunami.\par \par \uc2 Japan's solo actions drew criticism from the United States.\par \par \uc2 Japan has stayed out of the markets since then.\par \par \uc2 The yen has weakened to a 3-1/2 year low against the dollar in recent weeks on expectations for Prime Minister Shinzo Abe's policy mix of monetary and fiscal stimulus to end nearly two decades of stagnation and deflation.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tetsushi Kajimoto and Stanley White; Editing by \uc2 John Mair\uc2  and Stephen Coates)\par \par \uc2 JAPAN-ECONOMY/FURUSAWA (UPDATE 1) | ABN | D | E | RBN | J | M | NAT | U | RNP | DNP | PTD   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130328e93s001bi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
