\par\par \b \uc2 Tokyo Shares Fall As Japan Fin Min Comments Push Up Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kosaku Narioka   \par \uc2 409 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Februar 2013\par 07:32\par \uc2 Dow Jones Asian Equities Report\par \uc2 AER\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Tokyo stocks declined Tuesday with major exporters weighing on the Nikkei Stock Average as the yen strengthened after the Japanese finance minister dashed expectations for foreign bond buying as part of monetary easing.\par \par \uc2 The benchmark index fell 35.53 points, or 0.3%, to 11,372.34 following the prior session's 2.1% rise. The Topix index of all Tokyo Stock Exchange First Section issues added 0.92 points, or 0.1%, to 963.61, with 26 out of 33 subindexes ending in positive territory.\par \par \uc2 Shares remained under pressure during the day as the yen strengthened after Finance Minister Taro Aso said his government is not thinking about asking the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to consider buying foreign bonds - a step likely viewed as \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Kazumasa Iwata, a former Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor and one of leading candidates to be the next BOJ head, proposed last year the idea of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting up a Y50 trillion "crisis prevention fund" to invest in foreign securities.\par \par \uc2 "Even though there was no criticism against Japan over the recent yen weakening at the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2 , there will probably be a limit to policies Japan can now undertake," said Naoki Fujiwara, fund manager at Shinkin Asset Management. "The rest depends on how much of the recent yen weakening trickles down to the real economy, boosting corporate capital investment and so forth."\par \par \uc2 Major exporters ended mostly lower. \uc2 Tokyo Electron\uc2  fell 2.5% to Y4,140 and \uc2 Toyota Motor\uc2  dropped 0.9% to Y4,740.\par \par \uc2 Some domestic demand driven defensive stocks gained ground. Kao rose 2.1% to Y2,972, while \uc2 Kirin Holdings\uc2  added 4.4% to Y1,248.\par \par \uc2 Bucking the broader market trend, Bridgestone ascended 10% to Y2,820 after the firm said it expects its net profit to rise 37% to a record Y235 billion in 2013.\par \par \uc2 "That pace of profit growth is great," said Hideyuki Ishiguro, senior strategist at investment strategy at \uc2 Okasan Securities\uc2 . "There is no sense of overheating in the shares either. That was an outstanding outcome."\par \par \uc2 Bridgestone said a weaker yen has helped boost its bottom line despite concerns over the faltering economy in Europe.\par \par \uc2 March Nikkei 225 futures closed down 40 points, or 0.4%, at 11,370 on the Osaka Securities Exchange.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kosaku Narioka at kosaku.narioka@dowjones.com [ 19-02-13 0632GMT ]\par \par \uc2 4159 5011 55117   \par \par \uc2 Dokument AER0000020130219e92j0000b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw145\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2175\pichgoal600
