\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Britain's  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  chief riled by G7 mixed messages\b0\par\par\uc2 836 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2013\par 12:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 * Bank of England's King: Take G7 statement at face value\par \par \uc2 * Chides "so-called officials" for off-record briefing\par \par \uc2 * G20 chair Russia says important \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 (Adds UK prime minister, German government official)\par \par \uc2 By Clare Hutchison and Lidia Kelly\par \par \uc2 LONDON/MOSCOW, Feb 13 (Reuters) - A \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  statement designed to cool international \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  tensions should be taken at face value and anonymous officials should not try to reinterpret it, the Bank of England's chief said on Wednesday.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets were thrown in to turmoil on Tuesday after a day of mixed messages about exchange rates, prompted by Japan's new government pressing for an aggressive expansion of monetary policy, which has seen the yen weaken sharply.\par \par \uc2 G7 nations - Britain, the United States, Japan, Germany, France, Italy and Canada - said fiscal and monetary policies must be directed at domestic economies and not at targeting exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Japan quickly said the statement - released by Britain which chairs the G8 grouping (G7 plus Russia) this year - gave it a green light to continue efforts to reflate its economy.\par \par \uc2 But a G7 official responded by saying it was aimed squarely at Tokyo, a comment that prompt the yen to surge on a volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 Bank of England Governor \uc2 Mervyn King\uc2  said the statement should be taken at face value.\par \par \uc2 "When countries take measures to use monetary stimulus to support growth in their economies, then there will be exchange rate consequences and they should be allowed to flow through," King told a news conference.\par \par \uc2 "In the short run if you want to allow countries to stimulate growth, you have to allow them to take the measures of a monetary or other kind which will have consequences on the exchange rate, and we should let floating exchange rates take them where they will.\par \par \uc2 "When I put my name to that statement yesterday, I didn't expect that other so-called officials will be out there giving unattributable briefings ... trying to claim that the statement said what it didn't say."\par \par \uc2 Russia, chair of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  nations, said it was important that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese yen was definitely overvalued," Deputy Finance Minister Sergei Storchak told reporters, ahead of the G20 meeting in Moscow on Friday and Saturday.\par \par \uc2 Germany said the statement should draw a line under debate for now.\par \par \uc2 "I'm very glad that we have hopefully concluded the question of exchange rates for now ... which all G7 members accepted and I hope the G20 will also accept," a German government official told reporters.\par \par \uc2 A source familiar with the discussions that led to the release of the G7's first statement on exchange rates since 2011 said the off-record \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have been prompted by irritation that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had responded so quickly to say it had been given a clean bill of health.\par \par \uc2 ALL EYES ON G20\par \par \uc2 As a result, discussion at a G20 meeting of finance ministers and central bankers in Moscow at the end of the week may be more heated than previously expected with some concern about the pace at which the yen has fallen.\par \par \uc2 But officials said it was unlikely that Tokyo would face any sanction.\par \par \uc2 "To me the statement says - as long as price action is smooth (G7 officials) are not going to do anything. So I stand by my point that we are going to have more yen weakness in the medium-term," said Vasileios Gkionakis, head of global \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 UniCredit\uc2  in London.\par \par \uc2 Japan's top financial diplomat said his government will tell the G20 that its push to revive the economy with aggressive monetary expansion will benefit other nations and outweigh any possible negative effects.\par \par \uc2 "We share the view that each country should put their house in order by pursuing appropriate monetary, fiscal and structural policies and that would be the best contribution to the global economy," Takehiko Nakao, vice finance minister for international affairs, told Reuters in an interview.\par \par \uc2 U.S. and European officials have been concerned about comments from some Japanese officials that suggested Tokyo was targeting a specific level for the yen.\par \par \uc2 "You don't depreciate your way to growth whatever country you are," British Prime Minister \uc2 David Cameron\uc2  told parliament.\par \par \uc2 But \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  official Lael Brainard said on Monday that while competitive devaluations should be avoided, Washington supported Tokyo's efforts to reinvigorate growth and end deflation.\par \par \uc2 The U.S. Federal Reserve, like the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , has created vast amounts of new money to bolster its economy.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Annika Breidthardt, Tomasz Janowski, Tetsushi Kajimoto, Katya Golubkova and Nia Williams. Writing by Mike Peacock. Editing by Jeremy Gaunt.)\par \par \uc2 G7/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 2) | C | D | E | M | O | U | MTL | GRO | SOF | OIL | G | RBN | J | ABX | BNX | FUN | RNA | UKI | AFA | CSA | LBY | RWSA | RWS | REULB | GNS | Z | RNP | DNP | PGE   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020130213e92d000sl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
