\par\par \b \uc2 BOJ Hayami Opposed  \highlight22\uc2 Currency Intervention \highlight\uc2 , Foreign Bond Buying in 2002\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tatsuo Ito   \par \uc2 454 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Januar 2013\par 00:51\par \uc2 Dow Jones Global Equities News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2013 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Former Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Masaru Hayami opposed government \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen at a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy board meeting in 2002, as well as the idea the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying foreign bonds, according to detailed minutes of the meeting released Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Calls for "unlimited" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  were growing at the time as the dollar had fallen sharply to around Y116 from Y131 at the end of 2001, eating into exporters' profits and threatening Japan's export-dependent economy.\par \par \uc2 The BOJ unveils detailed minutes of past policy board meetings after 10 years. Mr. Hayami, known for favoring a strong yen, passed away in 2009 after serving as BOJ governor from March 1998 to March 2003.\par \par \uc2 The minutes may provide useful background for the current decision makers as they assess monetary policy and \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates in 2013.\par \par \uc2 At the 2002 meeting, Mr. Hayami said modest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  aimed at stabilizing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market was "fine," but he expressed doubts about massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to alter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates.\par \par \uc2 "No country is undertaking such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Mr. Hayami said, according to the minutes of the July 15-16, 2002 meeting.\par \par \uc2 Despite Mr. Hayami's opposition, the government later launched massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's rise, spending about Y35 trillion to buy dollars from January 2003 to March 2004.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Hayami also dismissed the idea of the BOJ buying foreign bonds, the minutes showed.\par \par \uc2 "It is really absurd to let the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buy foreign bonds" as the dollar's falls could leave the country with huge \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses, Mr. Hayami said. "Central banks shouldn't buy such assets."\par \par \uc2 The BOJ has typically shied away from foreign bond purchases. But the notion of the BOJ buying foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated bonds as part of its monetary easing came back into the spotlight in 2011 and 2012, when the yen resumed its rise.\par \par \uc2 Former Deputy Gov. Kazumasa Iwata, a candidate to succeed current Gov. \uc2 Masaaki Shirakawa\uc2 , whose term expires in April, proposed the idea of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  setting up a Y50 trillion "crisis prevention fund" to invest in foreign securities.\par \par \uc2 But the BOJ board opposed the move, saying the finance ministry had jurisdiction and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  should only act as an agent in this respect.\par \par \uc2 Heizo Takenaka, a former economy minister who attended the 2002 board meeting as a government representative, said active debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was "quite fresh" to him, and the subject should be taken up by a government panel on economy and fiscal policy, as it was important for economic strategy, the minutes said.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tatsuo Ito at tatsuo.ito@dowjones.com [ 28-01-13 2351GMT ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020130128e91s000xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
