\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Bundesbank Chief Warns Japan Not To 'Politicize' Rates\b0\par\par\uc2 595 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 2013\par 01:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2013, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 (From THE WALL STREET JOURNAL 1/22/13)\par \par \uc2 By Brian Blackstone\par \par \uc2 FRANKFURT -- Bundesbank President \uc2 Jens Weidmann\uc2  warned Japan not to "politicize" its exchange rate by pursuing an overly aggressive monetary policy, reflecting mounting concern in Europe that other central banks may cheapen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a means of stimulating economic growth.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government as well as Hungary's "are \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the duties of the central banks, pressuring for a more aggressive monetary policy" that threatens \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence, Mr. Weidmann said in a speech on Monday.\par \par \uc2 "A consequence, whether intended or not, could lead to an increasingly politicized exchange rate. Until now, the international monetary system has come through the crisis without a race to devaluation, and I really hope that it stays that way," Mr. Weidmann said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates are emerging as a central issue for global central bankers who are trying to jump-start ailing economies with little room to reduce interest rates. If countries outside the euro zone engage in these policies, it could drive the value of the euro higher, derailing recovery hopes by making European exports more expensive in global markets.\par \par \uc2 Japan's new government is pressing the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  to set a 2% inflation target, double its current objective. The prospect of aggressive monetary easing has in recent weeks pushed the yen lower against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  is expected to announce its new inflation target and additional asset purchases after its policy meeting on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Government-backed appointees to \uc2 Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  have ensured five straight months of rate cuts over the protests of the bank's governor and his deputies.\par \par \uc2 European officials have reacted with growing alarm as their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the euro, has risen. The euro gained nearly 7% against a wide basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  since late July, when European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  signaled that \uc2 the ECB\uc2  was willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in euro-zone government bond markets. It is up 10% against the U.S. dollar over that time frame.\par \par \uc2 The ECB\uc2 's bond plan calmed fears of a euro-zone breakup, boosting the euro. \uc2 The ECB\uc2  hasn't purchased any bonds yet, keeping its balance sheet steady. \uc2 The ECB\uc2  has resisted cutting interest rates near to zero as the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2  and \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  have done.\par \par \uc2 Jean-Claude Juncker, head of the euro-zone finance ministers' group, last week said the euro's value was "dangerously high." threatening the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bloc's recovery. German Finance Minister \uc2 Wolfgang Schauble\uc2  said he found Japan's policies "worrying."\par \par \uc2 ECB\uc2  officials have so far played down the euro's strength, and expect the bloc's economy -- which hasn't expanded since the third quarter of 2011 -- to recover later this year. \uc2 The ECB\uc2 's Mr. Draghi said at his monthly news conference on Jan. 10 that the euro is near its long-term average. Germany's export-reliant economy should recover this year, the Bundesbank said in its monthly report, citing improved prospects for exports.\par \par \uc2 But the effects of the higher euro could weigh on economies in Southern Europe such as Spain and Italy, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 These countries are trying to revamp their economies to cut labor costs and make their products more competitive in global markets. A higher exchange rate makes that process harder.\par \par \uc2 Bundesbank officials worry that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's policies could have a signaling effect to other central banks.\par \par \uc2 ---\par \par \uc2 Margit Feher contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 22-01-13 0043GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020130225e91m0010r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw200\pich25\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3000\pichgoal375
